1
00:02:20,606 --> 00:02:24,725
You keep yelling that you
are superior to everyone.

2
00:02:26,326 --> 00:02:28,205
You keep crying out.

3
00:02:30,566 --> 00:02:31,845
Well..

4
00:02:33,046 --> 00:02:35,125
This is the fighting field.

5
00:02:35,806 --> 00:02:38,405
Draw your sword and challenge me.

6
00:02:39,606 --> 00:02:43,005
So we will see...

7
00:02:44,086 --> 00:02:45,765
We will see...

8
00:02:47,766 --> 00:02:50,605
...how you learn by bitter experience.

9
00:02:51,086 --> 00:02:53,485
You're not even equal to me.

10
00:02:54,006 --> 00:02:55,845
How could you challenge me?

11
00:02:56,366 --> 00:03:00,125
They'd cut you into a
thousand pieces with my order.

12
00:03:00,446 --> 00:03:02,405
No.

13
00:03:03,246 --> 00:03:05,485
I'm neither afraid of death...

14
00:03:05,886 --> 00:03:08,405
...nor avoid my fate like you do.

15
00:03:09,326 --> 00:03:10,405
Well..

16
00:03:11,046 --> 00:03:12,685
My presence here...

17
00:03:13,886 --> 00:03:15,685
...is the proof.

18
00:03:16,446 --> 00:03:19,885
Well... This dog...

19
00:03:21,006 --> 00:03:22,485
This corpse...

20
00:03:24,006 --> 00:03:27,445
...should be a lesson for you people!

21
00:03:29,806 --> 00:03:31,045
Come on!

22
00:03:31,366 --> 00:03:33,245
Tell your dog to come for me!

23
00:03:33,686 --> 00:03:35,645
I can fight anyone here!

24
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:38,925
Altuga!

25
00:03:39,526 --> 00:03:41,085
Hristo!

26
00:03:42,366 --> 00:03:44,885
Avenge Lukas!

27
00:03:47,166 --> 00:03:48,565
Osman..

28
00:03:48,806 --> 00:03:52,525
You made my foolish brother your dog!

29
00:03:53,206 --> 00:03:56,925
-I'll throw your bones under his feet!
-We will see.

30
00:04:00,886 --> 00:04:03,205
Alps! Now!

31
00:04:18,846 --> 00:04:21,125
Captivity of Turks is over!

32
00:04:21,125 --> 00:04:23,125
We'll make their lives miserable now!

33
00:04:23,126 --> 00:04:25,685
My alps and I are ready for
any orders, my Shahzade.

34
00:04:25,686 --> 00:04:28,285
-It's time to slaughter those dastards.
-Someone's coming.

35
00:04:28,286 --> 00:04:30,285
We'll butcher whoever stands on our way!

36
00:04:44,446 --> 00:04:48,285
Whoever attempts to enslave
Turks will face death sooner or later!

37
00:04:48,406 --> 00:04:49,965
Let's go help father, brother.

38
00:04:50,086 --> 00:04:52,325
-Let's go!
-Let's go.

39
00:04:55,126 --> 00:04:56,685
Where did they come from?

40
00:04:56,926 --> 00:04:59,045
While Osman made noise here,

41
00:04:59,486 --> 00:05:02,205
...he placed his men among the local people.

42
00:05:02,366 --> 00:05:05,325
Osman... You will never give up.

43
00:05:14,766 --> 00:05:16,125
We're here, my Bey!

44
00:05:16,206 --> 00:05:18,365
We saved the prisoners, my Bey!

45
00:05:18,766 --> 00:05:22,085
Hit the heathens now! Cut off their tongues!

46
00:05:44,526 --> 00:05:48,085
Thank You, my Allah. Thank You.

47
00:06:46,406 --> 00:06:49,205
I won't let anyone but me kill you, Osman.

48
00:06:55,726 --> 00:06:57,925
Allah is the greatest!

49
00:08:26,886 --> 00:08:28,805
Damn it! What's going on?

50
00:08:30,526 --> 00:08:32,765
They're gone! They're all gone!

51
00:08:33,206 --> 00:08:35,125
Nokers, come with me.

52
00:08:41,006 --> 00:08:43,164
Osman Bey secret tents

53
00:08:49,446 --> 00:08:52,485
Easy, girl. You may burn yourself.

54
00:08:52,966 --> 00:08:56,765
You touched the herbs. That's
why this soup tastes so delicious.

55
00:08:57,086 --> 00:08:59,445
Wait, don't burn yourself.

56
00:09:01,366 --> 00:09:03,125
My mother's voice.

57
00:09:03,846 --> 00:09:06,485
It mixes with your voice, Bala.

58
00:09:08,046 --> 00:09:09,605
Why?

59
00:09:14,046 --> 00:09:16,645
Mother, what are you doing?

60
00:09:17,606 --> 00:09:19,845
We can do that. Give me the axe.

61
00:09:20,086 --> 00:09:22,245
We never let the elders work.

62
00:09:22,446 --> 00:09:26,285
Bala Hatun, may Allah be
pleased with you. I can do it myself.

63
00:09:26,446 --> 00:09:27,925
Don't bother.

64
00:09:28,086 --> 00:09:31,725
It won't bother me at all. Give it to me.

65
00:09:33,246 --> 00:09:38,405
How can we provide peace in our
state if our elders and sisters don't rest?

66
00:09:39,766 --> 00:09:41,565
We should support each other.

67
00:09:41,646 --> 00:09:44,805
-May Allah be pleased with you.
-In the name of Allah, the compassionate, the merciful

68
00:09:47,166 --> 00:09:49,445
Why are you so good?

69
00:09:52,886 --> 00:09:54,925
What my aunt told me...

70
00:09:57,446 --> 00:09:59,685
The woman who killed my family.

71
00:10:01,766 --> 00:10:05,365
My enemy... It can't be you.

72
00:10:22,526 --> 00:10:23,925
Damn it..

73
00:10:44,646 --> 00:10:46,005
Meryem..

74
00:10:47,446 --> 00:10:49,885
Do you still have a headache, my daughter?

75
00:10:51,886 --> 00:10:56,125
Maybe my grandmother's herbs would help.

76
00:10:56,926 --> 00:10:59,231
Come on, let me
rub your head a little.

77
00:10:59,243 --> 00:11:00,285
There is no need.

78
00:11:01,286 --> 00:11:03,765
I'll have some rest, then I will be alright.

79
00:11:05,806 --> 00:11:07,445
Alright. Have some rest.

80
00:11:29,086 --> 00:11:31,485
You affect me badly, Bala.

81
00:11:39,006 --> 00:11:42,845
You are harming me and...

82
00:11:43,686 --> 00:11:47,885
..my revenge.

83
00:11:48,206 --> 00:11:50,085
I shouldn't get close to you.

84
00:11:56,166 --> 00:11:57,805
Because of you...

85
00:11:59,926 --> 00:12:01,645
I betrayed my aunt.

86
00:12:36,086 --> 00:12:37,965
This road leads to Kurupinar.

87
00:12:38,766 --> 00:12:42,885
The trees in that area are so
dense that they block the view.

88
00:12:47,766 --> 00:12:51,205
Osman will use the trees as
a shield and escape, Ulugan.

89
00:12:51,806 --> 00:12:56,485
If necessary, I will burn the
whole forest that protects him...

90
00:12:56,486 --> 00:12:58,805
...and pick his bones from the ashes.

91
00:12:58,846 --> 00:13:01,845
But I will not let him escape. Come on.

92
00:13:22,206 --> 00:13:26,405
-Orhan, check and see if they are coming.
-As you order, my Bey.

93
00:14:17,566 --> 00:14:20,165
My Bey, they are not far away.

94
00:14:20,166 --> 00:14:24,645
They are coming in large numbers. It is
clear that Byzantium and Nokers have united.

95
00:14:25,886 --> 00:14:27,365
Why are we leaving, my Bey?

96
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:29,845
Give the order, let's ambush and kill them all.

97
00:14:29,846 --> 00:14:32,605
Let's take revenge for the martyrs.

98
00:14:33,286 --> 00:14:35,925
Don't act with blind courage.

99
00:14:36,686 --> 00:14:39,605
First, we will take our
measures, then we will attack.

100
00:14:40,566 --> 00:14:44,125
Now, they outnumber us

101
00:14:44,126 --> 00:14:46,405
I will hit them so hard that...

102
00:14:46,606 --> 00:14:48,605
...even Olcaytu
Khan will hear about it.

103
00:14:49,526 --> 00:14:51,005
God willing my Bey.

104
00:14:51,046 --> 00:14:53,205
My Bey, what are you planning?

105
00:14:53,646 --> 00:14:55,805
You will all hear it at the council.

106
00:14:57,926 --> 00:15:01,125
Kanyumaz. -My Bey.
-You go from the north.

107
00:15:01,206 --> 00:15:04,365
We will go from the south.
-As you order, my Bey.

108
00:15:04,366 --> 00:15:05,765
As you order, my Bey.

109
00:15:05,846 --> 00:15:07,325
We will mislead Ulugan.

110
00:15:07,326 --> 00:15:10,645
We will meet at the tribe! Come on!

111
00:15:48,766 --> 00:15:53,565
Your duty was to ensure the security
of the Arena, and what did you do?

112
00:15:54,806 --> 00:15:56,085
Nothing.

113
00:15:58,486 --> 00:15:59,525
And...

114
00:16:01,406 --> 00:16:03,325
Lukas died.

115
00:16:06,846 --> 00:16:11,885
Then why are you still alive?

116
00:16:17,806 --> 00:16:20,245
I have no patience...

117
00:16:22,006 --> 00:16:25,365
...for foolishness and defeat.

118
00:16:26,366 --> 00:16:28,925
Those who make mistakes will die.

119
00:16:29,886 --> 00:16:31,445
You will only...

120
00:16:31,646 --> 00:16:34,565
..serve our revenge.

121
00:16:34,566 --> 00:16:38,885
The revenge we will take from
Osman is growing day by day.

122
00:16:40,526 --> 00:16:41,725
Hristo.

123
00:16:48,886 --> 00:16:51,845
Report Lukas's death with this letter.

124
00:16:52,606 --> 00:16:57,045
Deliver it to the Emperor immediately.
-Yes ma'am.

125
00:17:02,526 --> 00:17:04,285
The great Emperor...

126
00:17:05,806 --> 00:17:09,525
...will want to turn this
place into hell for Lukas.

127
00:17:10,486 --> 00:17:13,805
We will prepare accordingly.

128
00:17:23,246 --> 00:17:24,565
Osman..

129
00:17:26,846 --> 00:17:30,525
...I will corner you in a way you cannot escape.

130
00:18:14,926 --> 00:18:16,245
Altuga...

131
00:18:17,246 --> 00:18:19,005
What do you hear? Tell us.

132
00:18:22,846 --> 00:18:24,285
Osman..

133
00:18:25,086 --> 00:18:27,485
His mind works like a wolf's, Ulugan.

134
00:18:27,726 --> 00:18:29,525
They have split into two.

135
00:18:29,846 --> 00:18:32,005
He wants to weaken us.

136
00:18:32,326 --> 00:18:34,725
He wants to make his tracks disappear.

137
00:18:36,006 --> 00:18:38,445
I will show him what strength is.

138
00:18:43,286 --> 00:18:45,845
Our fight will be fierce, Osman.

139
00:18:48,166 --> 00:18:49,525
Nokers...

140
00:18:50,046 --> 00:18:51,885
Byzantium soldiers.

141
00:18:52,366 --> 00:18:55,085
Even if you set the whole forest on fire...

142
00:18:55,206 --> 00:18:57,685
...or uproot the great trees...

143
00:18:57,686 --> 00:19:01,365
...you will find
Osman's den. Now, go

144
00:19:02,006 --> 00:19:03,845
We are going to the tribe.

145
00:19:04,446 --> 00:19:07,445
We cannot know where Osman will attack. Come on.

146
00:19:22,686 --> 00:19:24,565
Osman Bey Secret Tents

147
00:19:29,126 --> 00:19:32,565
Osman Bey is coming!

148
00:19:39,726 --> 00:19:41,485
Thanks to Allah!

149
00:19:41,526 --> 00:19:43,245
My father is here.

150
00:19:43,606 --> 00:19:46,045
They came here safely, thanks to Allah.

151
00:19:56,286 --> 00:19:59,565
-Peace be upon you!
-Peace be upon you, my Bey.

152
00:19:59,566 --> 00:20:02,405
Were those traitors punished, my Bey?

153
00:20:05,286 --> 00:20:07,245
My brave Alps...

154
00:20:07,366 --> 00:20:09,205
...my fearless sisters.

155
00:20:10,886 --> 00:20:12,965
Thanks to my Allah.

156
00:20:13,486 --> 00:20:17,805
The one who watered these
blessed lands with blood...

157
00:20:18,726 --> 00:20:23,045
...the one who dreamt of
destroying our glorious state...

158
00:20:23,686 --> 00:20:25,525
..and..

159
00:20:25,686 --> 00:20:28,205
...killed my unborn grandchild...

160
00:20:28,926 --> 00:20:31,045
...Byzantine's
Commander Lukas...

161
00:20:34,006 --> 00:20:35,925
...paid for what he did.

162
00:20:39,646 --> 00:20:41,125
He died as he deserved.

163
00:20:42,686 --> 00:20:47,885
Long live Osman Bey!

164
00:20:54,126 --> 00:20:56,965
The lands that shake under
the steps of the Turks...

165
00:20:58,126 --> 00:21:01,205
...the lands we made our
homeland with our blood...

166
00:21:01,526 --> 00:21:06,085
...will now be the grave for those who...

167
00:21:07,206 --> 00:21:09,925
...sent us away with betrayal...

168
00:21:10,246 --> 00:21:12,365
...for those who disrupted our unity.

169
00:21:15,766 --> 00:21:18,005
The swords we sharpened with revenge...

170
00:21:18,486 --> 00:21:20,165
...will strike the enemy's heart...

171
00:21:20,166 --> 00:21:22,325
...like a burning fire.

172
00:21:24,446 --> 00:21:25,965
O, my people!

173
00:21:27,046 --> 00:21:30,805
Know that the whole world...

174
00:21:31,926 --> 00:21:34,085
...expects a new rise from us.

175
00:21:41,126 --> 00:21:42,245
We will see..

176
00:21:43,406 --> 00:21:46,085
...Allah's justice as our guide...

177
00:21:47,126 --> 00:21:49,925
...and bring the order that they trampled on...

178
00:21:50,766 --> 00:21:52,565
..back.

179
00:21:56,286 --> 00:22:02,845
We will teach the world again that
Turks will never give up, never fall!

180
00:22:03,486 --> 00:22:14,565
Allah is the Greatest! Allah is the Greatest!

181
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:18,285
Osman Bey!

182
00:22:23,046 --> 00:22:25,565
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

183
00:22:25,566 --> 00:22:29,125
I informed everyone that Lukas dog died, my Bey.

184
00:22:29,126 --> 00:22:33,125
These are valiants who are eager
to stand by you in your da'wah.

185
00:22:33,846 --> 00:22:36,725
Thank you, valiants. Long live.

186
00:22:37,446 --> 00:22:41,325
-I want to see all the Beys in my tent.
-As you order, my Bey.

187
00:22:47,366 --> 00:22:49,245
My gazelle-eyed love...

188
00:22:49,726 --> 00:22:51,405
Are you tired, huh?

189
00:22:51,726 --> 00:22:53,165
No, I am alright.

190
00:22:54,166 --> 00:22:56,685
Every day you return home

191
00:22:56,726 --> 00:23:00,045
...peace fills my heart like the sun, Orhan.

192
00:23:00,086 --> 00:23:01,605
That peace...

193
00:23:02,406 --> 00:23:04,325
...shines from your eyes..

194
00:23:04,606 --> 00:23:06,685
...into my heart.

195
00:23:06,886 --> 00:23:09,165
It becomes a star in the dark nights...

196
00:23:09,326 --> 00:23:11,165
...and lights my way.

197
00:23:11,486 --> 00:23:13,285
It carries me...

198
00:23:13,286 --> 00:23:15,325
...and brings me to you, my Holofira.

199
00:23:18,286 --> 00:23:21,605
The heart that was once full of sorrow...

200
00:23:21,806 --> 00:23:24,245
...healed with your love, Orhan.

201
00:23:25,486 --> 00:23:27,725
What will I do if something happens to you?

202
00:23:29,606 --> 00:23:30,925
Thankfully...

203
00:23:31,126 --> 00:23:32,925
I am not alone anymore.

204
00:23:34,926 --> 00:23:38,525
-I will wait for you with our child.
-I know.

205
00:23:39,246 --> 00:23:40,525
Behind me...

206
00:23:40,926 --> 00:23:42,965
...I have people who await my return.

207
00:23:42,966 --> 00:23:44,645
I have you.

208
00:23:44,646 --> 00:23:46,325
No matter what happens...

209
00:23:46,366 --> 00:23:49,605
..I will always return my Holofira. Always.

210
00:23:50,646 --> 00:23:52,725
Now tell me...

211
00:23:53,046 --> 00:23:56,165
...has my baby, my child...

212
00:23:56,246 --> 00:23:58,525
...been a good companion?

213
00:23:58,766 --> 00:24:00,245
Sure it has.

214
00:24:00,286 --> 00:24:03,685
It's a good companion but just like you...

215
00:24:03,686 --> 00:24:05,845
...it does not know how to stay still.

216
00:24:05,846 --> 00:24:07,685
Is that so?

217
00:24:09,446 --> 00:24:10,805
Don't worry...

218
00:24:11,206 --> 00:24:12,965
Gonca is always with me.

219
00:24:13,526 --> 00:24:14,805
Gonca Hatun.

220
00:24:20,926 --> 00:24:22,125
Thank you.

221
00:24:23,046 --> 00:24:25,645
I've heard you always stay with Holofira.

222
00:24:25,766 --> 00:24:28,005
I don't know how we can repay you.

223
00:24:28,446 --> 00:24:30,005
As long as you are here...

224
00:24:30,006 --> 00:24:32,885
...I won't have to worry about my Hatun.

225
00:24:33,286 --> 00:24:34,525
Thank you.

226
00:24:35,166 --> 00:24:36,965
Holofira is my sister.

227
00:24:38,326 --> 00:24:40,645
And your child is my nephew, Orhan Bey.

228
00:24:41,286 --> 00:24:45,285
If I don't protect Holofira
in this tribe, then who will?

229
00:24:45,886 --> 00:24:46,925
Besides..

230
00:24:49,406 --> 00:24:51,045
...I understand her fear...

231
00:24:52,006 --> 00:24:56,845
...and worries better than anyone.

232
00:24:58,726 --> 00:24:59,885
Thank you.

233
00:25:00,326 --> 00:25:01,605
Long live.

234
00:25:02,086 --> 00:25:03,525
Long live.

235
00:25:04,806 --> 00:25:06,165
Come on Holofira.

236
00:25:11,526 --> 00:25:13,885
May you be in peace where you lie, my baby.

237
00:25:20,326 --> 00:25:21,965
My hatun..

238
00:25:22,926 --> 00:25:24,685
My rosebud

239
00:25:28,126 --> 00:25:30,085
The dastard..

240
00:25:31,526 --> 00:25:35,485
...who killed our baby and
broke our happiness passed away.

241
00:25:39,086 --> 00:25:41,445
May he burn in flames, Alaaddin.

242
00:25:41,926 --> 00:25:44,125
I hope...

243
00:25:45,246 --> 00:25:47,565
...Allah will give him...

244
00:25:48,246 --> 00:25:51,005
...much worse than what he did to us.

245
00:25:51,166 --> 00:25:52,725
God willing.

246
00:25:57,326 --> 00:26:00,245
Don't fill your heart with grief, my dear.

247
00:26:01,926 --> 00:26:04,045
We need to be strong.

248
00:26:06,766 --> 00:26:10,325
My children and nephews will
grow up together, God willing.

249
00:26:13,086 --> 00:26:16,085
God willing, my Alaaddin. God willing.

250
00:26:24,246 --> 00:26:27,005
How could you let Osman escape?

251
00:26:27,246 --> 00:26:28,965
With all those nokers...

252
00:26:29,886 --> 00:26:31,805
All those soldiers...

253
00:26:34,006 --> 00:26:35,485
How could you do that?

254
00:26:49,726 --> 00:26:53,405
How are you to question me?

255
00:26:57,286 --> 00:27:00,325
I'd cut off your poor head.

256
00:27:01,126 --> 00:27:04,005
The arrow is off the bow, Ulugan.

257
00:27:05,166 --> 00:27:07,845
I don't care about my life anymore.

258
00:27:08,606 --> 00:27:11,325
I need blood.

259
00:27:11,886 --> 00:27:13,965
I need vengeance.

260
00:27:14,566 --> 00:27:17,605
Osman's alps and family have been encouraged.

261
00:27:18,006 --> 00:27:20,205
If we turn against each other now.

262
00:27:20,566 --> 00:27:22,405
...Osman will destroy us.

263
00:27:30,846 --> 00:27:35,005
What? Are you afraid, Kayi boy?

264
00:27:36,446 --> 00:27:38,605
Afraid of death?

265
00:27:38,846 --> 00:27:40,605
I'm never afraid of Osman.

266
00:27:40,806 --> 00:27:43,245
This is all because of you, Ilbay.

267
00:27:44,166 --> 00:27:47,645
We relied on your wife's brother.

268
00:27:48,206 --> 00:27:49,805
And we got deceived.

269
00:27:54,366 --> 00:27:56,965
And this red woman's spy as well.

270
00:27:57,166 --> 00:27:59,925
My spy didn't betray.

271
00:28:25,886 --> 00:28:28,005
This is my final talk to you.

272
00:28:29,726 --> 00:28:32,125
If you make another mistake

273
00:28:32,206 --> 00:28:36,405
...your heads won't stay over your shoulders.

274
00:28:39,566 --> 00:28:41,845
Find Osman immediately.

275
00:28:41,966 --> 00:28:46,325
Otherwise, I'll bury you
three in the same grave.

276
00:28:59,246 --> 00:29:03,085
You have to tell me where
your master hides, brother.

277
00:29:03,366 --> 00:29:05,605
You have to tell. Come on.

278
00:29:05,966 --> 00:29:07,645
Leave my father, dastard!

279
00:29:07,806 --> 00:29:11,645
What kind of brother are you?
What kind of brother are you?

280
00:29:17,486 --> 00:29:19,325
Where is Osman, brother?

281
00:29:19,926 --> 00:29:22,045
Tell me where Osman is.

282
00:29:22,286 --> 00:29:26,565
Speak! I don't want to kill you
in front of your son. Come on!

283
00:29:27,246 --> 00:29:30,245
I won't speak even if you skin me.

284
00:29:34,206 --> 00:29:35,925
Lukas today.

285
00:29:36,406 --> 00:29:37,885
Ulugan tomorrow.

286
00:29:38,606 --> 00:29:40,965
The circle tightens, Altuga.

287
00:29:42,286 --> 00:29:45,565
Osman will be the hell for the cruel!

288
00:29:46,606 --> 00:29:49,565
Whoever stands beside the dog called Ulugan...

289
00:29:49,886 --> 00:29:52,525
...will burn to ashes one by one.

290
00:29:55,606 --> 00:29:57,365
And you..

291
00:29:59,766 --> 00:30:01,045
Look.

292
00:30:02,206 --> 00:30:03,845
Brother.

293
00:30:04,846 --> 00:30:06,085
Look.

294
00:30:06,486 --> 00:30:10,365
You have time until tomorrow.

295
00:30:13,606 --> 00:30:17,365
-Otherwise...
-Otherwise?

296
00:30:18,606 --> 00:30:20,685
Otherwise?

297
00:30:23,926 --> 00:30:26,645
You can't scare me with death.

298
00:30:31,566 --> 00:30:34,965
Come on, kill me.

299
00:30:36,486 --> 00:30:39,645
To serve a vile dog

300
00:30:40,366 --> 00:30:42,365
..kill me.

301
00:30:43,326 --> 00:30:44,845
That would suit you.

302
00:31:06,646 --> 00:31:08,485
Ghazi.

303
00:31:10,406 --> 00:31:12,165
Make your father come around.

304
00:31:12,606 --> 00:31:14,325
Make him speak.

305
00:31:15,606 --> 00:31:19,285
Otherwise I will cut off
both of your heads tomorrow.

306
00:31:23,686 --> 00:31:27,165
I swear on the spirit of my almighty father...

307
00:31:28,366 --> 00:31:30,325
...that I will do it.

308
00:31:38,246 --> 00:31:40,205
Ghazi.

309
00:31:41,126 --> 00:31:45,325
Ghazi... Ghazi.
Father, father.

310
00:31:45,726 --> 00:31:49,125
Go away, dastards! Dogs!

311
00:31:49,286 --> 00:31:53,365
-Dastards.
-Father, are you alright?

312
00:31:53,566 --> 00:31:57,685
-I'm fine, boy. I'm fine.
-Father.

313
00:31:58,046 --> 00:31:59,805
I'm fine.

314
00:32:00,006 --> 00:32:04,205
Many traitors once among us...

315
00:32:04,766 --> 00:32:10,045
...and many enemies got united against us.

316
00:32:10,206 --> 00:32:13,285
But the one in the right path...

317
00:32:13,566 --> 00:32:15,405
...has always become victorious.

318
00:32:15,686 --> 00:32:18,685
-Thank Allah, my Bey.
-Thanks to Allah, my Bey.

319
00:32:18,766 --> 00:32:21,725
Now we know what to do.

320
00:32:22,246 --> 00:32:26,045
We'll clear the dark clouds over our state.

321
00:32:26,366 --> 00:32:28,605
The weapons we took from Mongolians.

322
00:32:29,846 --> 00:32:32,965
The alps Yusuf Bey sent for us.

323
00:32:33,566 --> 00:32:38,845
They will be the key of the lock
they built against Kayi's freedom.

324
00:32:39,886 --> 00:32:43,045
For sure, we have both
alps and weapons, my Bey.

325
00:32:43,126 --> 00:32:46,683
But I don't know if that's
enough to attack the tribe.

326
00:32:46,695 --> 00:32:47,885
No.

327
00:32:48,406 --> 00:32:53,005
We won't attack the tribe
as the heathens expect.

328
00:32:54,246 --> 00:32:55,845
We'll capture Sogut.

329
00:32:55,846 --> 00:32:59,445
You say the wildfire of Kayi
will burn in Kayi first, huh?

330
00:32:59,646 --> 00:33:01,725
It will be so.

331
00:33:04,846 --> 00:33:08,885
You say the enemy expect us
to attack the tribe, huh, my Bey?

332
00:33:09,606 --> 00:33:11,245
What's the plan, father?

333
00:33:11,566 --> 00:33:14,245
How will we distract the dog called Ulugan?

334
00:33:14,246 --> 00:33:17,645
You and Orhan will split up and...

335
00:33:17,646 --> 00:33:21,805
...attack the spot where
Mongolians stay near the tribe.

336
00:33:22,006 --> 00:33:25,525
So Ulugan and his dogs will
think our next target is the tribe...

337
00:33:25,886 --> 00:33:28,325
...and take defense formation.

338
00:33:28,726 --> 00:33:32,165
Maybe, they'll never get out of there?
-God willing.

339
00:33:32,406 --> 00:33:34,125
God willing, son.

340
00:33:34,526 --> 00:33:39,645
Boran, alps and I will try to
open the smallest of the tunnels...

341
00:33:39,966 --> 00:33:43,285
...leading to Sogut which we sealed earlier.

342
00:33:43,566 --> 00:33:47,685
In the meantime, you'll
have finished your duty, sons.

343
00:33:48,126 --> 00:33:49,525
As you order, my Bey.

344
00:33:49,926 --> 00:33:52,125
Everybody knows their duties.

345
00:33:53,326 --> 00:33:55,125
Here we go.

346
00:34:12,005 --> 00:34:13,685
Fatma Hatun.

347
00:34:15,886 --> 00:34:17,364
Fatma Hatun.

348
00:34:46,726 --> 00:34:48,284
Meryem.

349
00:34:49,726 --> 00:34:51,445
Hatuns made sherbet.

350
00:34:51,606 --> 00:34:55,645
It feels good to drink before sleep.
-Well thought.

351
00:34:55,806 --> 00:34:57,805
We can drink together.

352
00:35:32,726 --> 00:35:36,045
What's the matter, Bala?
What are you thinking about?

353
00:35:38,526 --> 00:35:40,485
Lukas is dead now.

354
00:35:41,206 --> 00:35:44,525
They'll get more furious and attack, my Bey.

355
00:35:44,686 --> 00:35:46,125
No.

356
00:35:46,646 --> 00:35:49,765
It's good that the vile dog is dead.

357
00:35:49,926 --> 00:35:53,365
Our people got encouraged and confident.

358
00:35:56,046 --> 00:36:01,445
People and alps never lost
their trust in you, my Bey.

359
00:36:02,926 --> 00:36:05,205
You did everything for them.

360
00:36:05,686 --> 00:36:09,685
Everyone, from the eldest to babies, knows this.

361
00:36:09,726 --> 00:36:13,805
Yes. You're right. Well...

362
00:36:15,206 --> 00:36:18,325
Were you never afraid that we would fail?

363
00:36:19,926 --> 00:36:22,685
No. Why would I be?

364
00:36:23,526 --> 00:36:27,765
You don't know what being
Osman Bey's wife means.

365
00:36:29,766 --> 00:36:32,485
What does it mean? Let me know.

366
00:36:34,526 --> 00:36:36,845
It's such a thing...

367
00:36:37,326 --> 00:36:41,245
...that neither disasters
nor enemies can scare me.

368
00:36:41,286 --> 00:36:42,365
I know this.

369
00:36:42,486 --> 00:36:45,245
If Osman the Brunette says he'll come.

370
00:36:45,526 --> 00:36:48,685
...he will come to his Bala no matter what.

371
00:36:49,566 --> 00:36:54,045
He comes for help wherever
he is and whatever he's doing.

372
00:36:54,646 --> 00:37:00,045
He'll never me, his sons or his state.

373
00:37:00,286 --> 00:37:04,445
-What a man Osman the Brunette is!
-Yes.

374
00:37:04,886 --> 00:37:09,485
You should see Osman the
Brunette from my eyes just for once.

375
00:37:14,846 --> 00:37:16,405
Bala.

376
00:37:19,446 --> 00:37:24,285
Bala, stop. I'm here. Why are you doing this?

377
00:37:24,686 --> 00:37:27,485
I just hurt my feet. I didn't fall weak.

378
00:37:27,726 --> 00:37:29,805
This is not my first time.

379
00:37:38,206 --> 00:37:42,165
Come here. Come to me.

380
00:37:42,966 --> 00:37:45,445
Come here, over here.

381
00:37:48,286 --> 00:37:51,765
You should see yourself from my eyes, in fact.

382
00:37:53,526 --> 00:37:55,285
What am I like?

383
00:37:55,606 --> 00:37:57,085
Come closer.

384
00:37:57,446 --> 00:37:59,725
Come closer to me.

385
00:38:00,886 --> 00:38:03,205
You..

386
00:38:04,766 --> 00:38:08,085
You're the mountain I'm leaning on.

387
00:38:09,046 --> 00:38:12,285
You're my harbor in my hard times.

388
00:38:16,326 --> 00:38:17,525
My moon.

389
00:38:17,886 --> 00:38:20,085
My day and night.

390
00:38:20,966 --> 00:38:22,885
You are my heart.

391
00:38:24,166 --> 00:38:27,325
You were always with me. Always.

392
00:38:28,086 --> 00:38:32,085
When I swung swords and fought the heathens.

393
00:38:32,566 --> 00:38:35,085
...I always had you in my mind.

394
00:38:37,126 --> 00:38:39,125
Oh my strong wife...

395
00:38:40,646 --> 00:38:45,885
Since the day you said yes
to me, you have suffered a lot.

396
00:38:47,886 --> 00:38:50,685
Your tears have never stop running down.

397
00:38:54,406 --> 00:38:58,685
Compared to your sufferings,
mine means nothing, Osman.

398
00:38:59,446 --> 00:39:02,045
I vowed to be with you.

399
00:39:02,606 --> 00:39:06,165
As long as you are with
me, I'm ready for anything.

400
00:39:06,886 --> 00:39:08,965
Just be with me.

401
00:39:12,446 --> 00:39:15,965
Your absence burns me like fire.

402
00:39:16,686 --> 00:39:19,245
It burns me to ashes, Osman.
-Oh...

403
00:39:20,046 --> 00:39:25,405
Speaking of the ashes, stop there.
You should know the ashes inside me.

404
00:39:25,846 --> 00:39:28,525
You are my accepted prayer.

405
00:39:28,886 --> 00:39:31,525
All my burdens get lighter with you.

406
00:39:32,046 --> 00:39:34,525
May Allah never let me see your absence.

407
00:39:35,446 --> 00:39:37,405
May He never let me see your absence.

408
00:39:37,686 --> 00:39:39,645
Yours either, my Osman.

409
00:39:40,046 --> 00:39:41,885
Yours either.

410
00:39:48,166 --> 00:39:51,805
Come on, father. We'll get out of here.

411
00:39:52,366 --> 00:39:54,045
Come on.

412
00:39:56,166 --> 00:39:58,805
Of course we'll get out, son.

413
00:39:58,806 --> 00:40:00,325
Remember.

414
00:40:01,286 --> 00:40:04,365
Cerkutay never dies.

415
00:40:06,046 --> 00:40:08,805
Don't confuse your mind, Cerkutay.

416
00:40:09,126 --> 00:40:12,885
It's impossible for your to escape.

417
00:40:13,086 --> 00:40:15,085
Ghazi, stay behind me.

418
00:40:20,526 --> 00:40:23,085
Escape?

419
00:40:23,766 --> 00:40:28,125
This place won't be your
home but only your grave.

420
00:40:30,166 --> 00:40:32,845
I'll take your hopes...

421
00:40:33,286 --> 00:40:35,285
...out of your unbreakable souls!

422
00:40:36,366 --> 00:40:39,045
You won't find peace even for a single day.

423
00:40:42,006 --> 00:40:46,125
Your son Ghazi will remember you as a traitor.

424
00:40:46,406 --> 00:40:48,245
He'll be raised as a Mongolian.

425
00:40:48,486 --> 00:40:52,165
Nokers, take Ghazi.

426
00:40:56,486 --> 00:40:59,925
Father! Get off!
-Ghazi!

427
00:41:00,006 --> 00:41:04,605
Ghazi! Ghazi! I'll kill you!

428
00:41:04,686 --> 00:41:08,925
I swear I'll kill you! I swear I will kill you!

429
00:41:09,126 --> 00:41:12,365
With your death, I will wipe out the shame...

430
00:41:13,766 --> 00:41:16,925
...you put on us with your betrayal, Cerkutay.

431
00:41:17,006 --> 00:41:22,565
Father! Father! No!

432
00:41:23,366 --> 00:41:25,125
No!

433
00:41:25,366 --> 00:41:28,565
Don't die! Dont' die!

434
00:41:30,926 --> 00:41:32,845
No! No!

435
00:41:34,926 --> 00:41:37,805
Father! Father!

436
00:41:39,366 --> 00:41:41,445
Father!

437
00:41:44,966 --> 00:41:47,725
Die, you dastard!

438
00:41:48,766 --> 00:41:51,885
No! No!

439
00:42:07,806 --> 00:42:09,045
Ghazi..

440
00:42:10,686 --> 00:42:11,885
Ghazi..

441
00:42:17,086 --> 00:42:20,885
Father... -Ghazi..

442
00:42:22,766 --> 00:42:24,285
Ghazi..

443
00:42:34,486 --> 00:42:37,805
I seek forgiveness in Allah!

444
00:42:53,926 --> 00:42:55,885
Please, my Allah...

445
00:42:57,486 --> 00:43:00,365
Please, help, my Allah...

446
00:43:00,366 --> 00:43:03,685
Please my Allah...

447
00:43:04,006 --> 00:43:06,565
Take from my life and
give it to them, my Allah...

448
00:43:06,566 --> 00:43:08,525
Take from my years...

449
00:43:08,526 --> 00:43:12,145
My Allah, do not test me with their absence...

450
00:43:28,766 --> 00:43:30,605
Send word to Sofia.

451
00:43:30,606 --> 00:43:33,365
I need to talk to her. -From Sofia.

452
00:43:42,606 --> 00:43:45,645
Poena, I knew you would come here.

453
00:43:45,646 --> 00:43:50,445
I still don't know how Osman found
out we were going to attack, but...

454
00:43:50,446 --> 00:43:52,725
...I am sure you did not do this. You are...

455
00:43:52,726 --> 00:43:56,525
...not a person who would protect
the ones who killed your family...

456
00:43:56,526 --> 00:43:59,805
...you would not betray your parents.

457
00:43:59,806 --> 00:44:01,205
Right, Poena?

458
00:44:01,206 --> 00:44:04,765
You would never let your family down, right?

459
00:44:04,766 --> 00:44:05,805
My little bird...

460
00:44:05,806 --> 00:44:08,285
Don't you ever fool me.

461
00:44:08,286 --> 00:44:09,925
When the sun rises...

462
00:44:09,926 --> 00:44:13,805
...bring Bala to the riverside. I trust you.

463
00:44:18,806 --> 00:44:22,285
You trust me aunt.

464
00:44:22,286 --> 00:44:26,765
But I betrayed you.

465
00:44:27,126 --> 00:44:28,325
I betrayed my family...

466
00:44:29,126 --> 00:44:30,205
..you..

467
00:44:31,766 --> 00:44:34,645
...and my revenge.

468
00:44:36,126 --> 00:44:37,805
But I had to.

469
00:44:40,726 --> 00:44:42,725
I owed them a life.

470
00:44:51,006 --> 00:44:54,885
When the sun rises, bring Bala to the riverside.

471
00:44:54,886 --> 00:44:56,565
I trust you.

472
00:45:29,046 --> 00:45:31,685
They stay close to the entrance of the tunnel.

473
00:45:31,726 --> 00:45:33,965
These are patrol nokers, my Bey.

474
00:45:34,486 --> 00:45:36,165
Let's wait for them to leave.

475
00:45:36,366 --> 00:45:38,843
If they hear the noise,
more will come from around.

476
00:45:38,855 --> 00:45:39,685
No.

477
00:45:39,686 --> 00:45:42,645
We need to open the tunnel before Orhan arrives.

478
00:45:42,846 --> 00:45:46,765
We will attack them suddenly and kill them all.

479
00:45:46,766 --> 00:45:48,125
As you order, my Bey.

480
00:45:51,726 --> 00:45:52,885
Alps.

481
00:45:54,126 --> 00:45:56,165
Now. Walk!

482
00:46:12,886 --> 00:46:15,850
Let alone a single inch
of this land, even the preys of...

483
00:46:15,862 --> 00:46:18,725
...these lands are forbidden
for you, you infidel dogs.

484
00:46:19,206 --> 00:46:20,645
Remove their corpses.

485
00:46:20,646 --> 00:46:24,045
Otherwise, they will realize
that we are sneaking into the city.

486
00:46:24,046 --> 00:46:25,805
Alps, the duty is yours.

487
00:46:32,206 --> 00:46:33,925
Light the torches.

488
00:46:44,486 --> 00:46:45,645
Give it to me.

489
00:47:14,966 --> 00:47:16,165
My Bey...

490
00:47:16,526 --> 00:47:19,685
When we were closing the
passages leading to Sogut...

491
00:47:20,206 --> 00:47:22,565
...we used quite a lot of flying flames.

492
00:47:24,326 --> 00:47:27,205
My concern is that...

493
00:47:27,526 --> 00:47:29,325
...despite all this effort...

494
00:47:29,766 --> 00:47:33,045
...what if we can't reach the
end of the passage my Bey?

495
00:47:33,206 --> 00:47:35,485
What will we do then? -No.

496
00:47:35,926 --> 00:47:39,525
No Boran. We will. We need to open it.

497
00:47:39,526 --> 00:47:44,365
My Bey, we will not give
up. We will open it. But...

498
00:47:44,886 --> 00:47:48,685
The tunnel is quite long. And also,
it's closed off at every point, my Bey.

499
00:47:49,486 --> 00:47:53,125
-Did you give up hope, Boran?
-I would never, my Bey.

500
00:47:55,086 --> 00:48:02,205
Do you think it's easy for the state to revive
and for the nation to regain its freedom?

501
00:48:03,646 --> 00:48:08,405
If necessary, we will dig
here until our picks break...

502
00:48:08,406 --> 00:48:13,925
...and if necessary, until our nails are
pulled out and the skin of our hands is torn.

503
00:48:14,206 --> 00:48:18,365
We must take Sogut. You
will never fall into despair.

504
00:48:18,846 --> 00:48:20,525
Okay, my Bey.

505
00:48:20,526 --> 00:48:23,925
For sure, for sure We will take it.

506
00:48:24,246 --> 00:48:25,565
We will dig.

507
00:48:26,206 --> 00:48:27,485
Come on now.

508
00:48:28,726 --> 00:48:29,965
Come on.

509
00:48:29,966 --> 00:48:31,685
Let's start digging!

510
00:48:32,366 --> 00:48:34,805
-Allah is Eternal!
-Allah is The Righteous!

511
00:48:36,886 --> 00:48:41,325
Here, brother. My Allah, let us defeat them.

512
00:48:42,246 --> 00:49:00,325
-Allah is Eternal!
-Allah is The Righteous!

513
00:49:13,126 --> 00:49:17,285
What did you do to..

514
00:49:18,646 --> 00:49:21,845
...my tribe, my people...

515
00:49:21,846 --> 00:49:23,925
...my children?!

516
00:49:24,286 --> 00:49:26,085
You infidels!

517
00:49:28,886 --> 00:49:30,965
What did you want from them?

518
00:49:31,446 --> 00:49:32,925
What did they do to you?

519
00:49:33,366 --> 00:49:35,045
What did they do?

520
00:49:35,446 --> 00:49:41,565
-Allah is Eternal!
-Allah is The Righteous!

521
00:49:55,206 --> 00:49:57,885
-Is everyone ready?
-Yes my Shahzade.

522
00:49:57,886 --> 00:50:02,853
Our Alps are waiting for your
orders to send these dogs to hell.

523
00:50:02,865 --> 00:50:04,525
Okay.

524
00:50:04,526 --> 00:50:09,525
They are so confident in themselves that
death will catch them before they even notice.

525
00:50:14,286 --> 00:50:16,685
The area around the headquarters.

526
00:50:17,046 --> 00:50:19,205
It's surrounded by traps.

527
00:50:19,886 --> 00:50:22,965
These dogs' confidence comes from there.

528
00:50:23,206 --> 00:50:25,725
Are there traps? Where?

529
00:50:25,726 --> 00:50:27,645
Between the guards.

530
00:50:28,166 --> 00:50:31,245
They are walking a longer
path to avoid stepping on it.

531
00:50:31,246 --> 00:50:32,605
From where will we attack?

532
00:50:32,606 --> 00:50:35,125
We will attack the guards.

533
00:50:36,166 --> 00:50:37,445
Are you ready Ekrem Bey?

534
00:50:37,446 --> 00:50:40,685
Turks are always ready
for a battle, my Shahzade.

535
00:50:40,926 --> 00:50:44,245
-Sure. Aykurt. 
-My Shahzade.

536
00:50:44,686 --> 00:50:46,205
Give them the sign.

537
00:50:52,126 --> 00:50:54,005
Trap!

538
00:50:54,486 --> 00:50:56,725
The Righteous!

539
00:50:59,446 --> 00:51:03,205
Come on! Come on!

540
00:51:24,526 --> 00:51:26,245
Allah is the Greatest!

541
00:51:52,806 --> 00:51:55,645
Allah is the Greatest!

542
00:51:59,086 --> 00:52:02,965
Ulugan will lose his mind
when he hears about the raid.

543
00:52:02,966 --> 00:52:06,285
Anyone who fights against Osman
Bey will never find peace, brother.

544
00:52:06,286 --> 00:52:10,165
Now, he will take precautions
at the tribe out of fear.

545
00:52:10,166 --> 00:52:12,913
And with Allah's permission,
we will take Sogut, God willing.

546
00:52:12,925 --> 00:52:13,845
God willing.

547
00:52:13,846 --> 00:52:17,485
Now, gather the weapons
and set the headquarters on fire.

548
00:52:17,486 --> 00:52:22,645
Nothing belonging to these
dogs will remain in this land.

549
00:52:22,686 --> 00:52:24,925
As you order my Shahzade. Come on.

550
00:52:31,806 --> 00:52:33,445
Mongol Headquarters

551
00:52:42,526 --> 00:52:43,645
Come on!

552
00:52:46,326 --> 00:52:48,845
There is a lot to do! Hurry!

553
00:52:48,846 --> 00:52:51,125
-Allah is Eternal!
-Allah is The Righteous!

554
00:52:51,126 --> 00:52:52,925
Trap!

555
00:52:56,446 --> 00:52:59,845
The wolf has arrived.
The jackal's reign is over.

556
00:52:59,846 --> 00:53:01,725
Now it is time to pay the price!

557
00:53:01,726 --> 00:53:04,005
Ya Allah!

558
00:53:14,926 --> 00:53:17,805
Protect the prisoners!
Allah is the Greatest!

559
00:53:28,206 --> 00:53:30,245
Allah is the Greatest!

560
00:53:49,446 --> 00:53:53,445
Destroy this place! Don't let anyone escape!

561
00:54:01,286 --> 00:54:05,685
Allah is Eternal!

562
00:54:15,686 --> 00:54:19,565
This rock... It carries all the
load that blocks the passage.

563
00:54:19,566 --> 00:54:22,965
If we remove it, our path will open.

564
00:54:23,726 --> 00:54:25,525
God willing my Bey, God willing.

565
00:54:42,566 --> 00:54:43,805
Boran...

566
00:54:44,566 --> 00:54:46,485
It doesn't seem like it will work.

567
00:54:47,606 --> 00:54:49,525
It does not seem like it will move.

568
00:54:50,006 --> 00:54:53,485
Forget it. We will keep digging.

569
00:54:54,646 --> 00:54:58,565
Look, you're very tired.
Take a rest for a while.

570
00:54:58,566 --> 00:54:59,885
Yes, my Bey.

571
00:55:00,246 --> 00:55:01,405
Alps!

572
00:55:02,046 --> 00:55:03,885
Come on, it's your turn now.

573
00:55:12,726 --> 00:55:15,805
Stop, stop brother.

574
00:55:16,286 --> 00:55:17,765
Stop.

575
00:55:21,166 --> 00:55:24,525
My Allah, give me strength.

576
00:55:25,926 --> 00:55:28,725
Make me dust under my Bey's feet..

577
00:55:30,406 --> 00:55:36,445
...but give me the power to open this tunnel.

578
00:55:36,846 --> 00:55:38,485
In the name of Allah.

579
00:55:38,486 --> 00:55:40,525
Come on.

580
00:55:42,966 --> 00:55:44,085
Allah.

581
00:56:01,326 --> 00:56:03,445
Move!

582
00:56:21,886 --> 00:56:23,965
Is there any trace, Altuga?

583
00:56:25,206 --> 00:56:27,605
From sunrise to sunset...

584
00:56:28,166 --> 00:56:31,045
...we rode our horses all
night. Commander Ulugan.

585
00:56:33,526 --> 00:56:37,925
We didn't see any smoke or fire.

586
00:56:37,926 --> 00:56:40,005
We found no trace of Osman.

587
00:56:43,086 --> 00:56:47,525
Go, don't come back to me until you find Osman.

588
00:56:54,686 --> 00:56:57,605
No food, no water.

589
00:56:58,526 --> 00:57:00,405
You won't even sleep!

590
00:57:00,926 --> 00:57:02,805
Get lost!

591
00:57:14,806 --> 00:57:16,725
Red Hatun.

592
00:57:17,926 --> 00:57:24,405
Ilbay and his wife. You will
search for Osman everywhere.

593
00:57:25,726 --> 00:57:28,965
You wanted revenge go and take it!

594
00:57:29,126 --> 00:57:32,045
I work alone, Ulugan.

595
00:57:34,846 --> 00:57:37,445
I don't want to carry a burden with me.

596
00:57:37,446 --> 00:57:41,245
Sofia, don't think I am like others.

597
00:57:42,086 --> 00:57:43,965
I have no friends.

598
00:57:43,966 --> 00:57:46,245
And my enemy does not live either.

599
00:57:46,766 --> 00:57:50,085
Stop fighting like dogs among yourselves.

600
00:57:53,846 --> 00:57:58,245
If you can't find Osman,
you better get ready to die.

601
00:58:09,046 --> 00:58:10,445
Ah Ulugan.

602
00:58:11,886 --> 00:58:17,485
If you can't find Osman, how
will you answer to Olcaytu?

603
00:58:38,246 --> 00:58:42,045
Ilbay, this devil will do something.

604
00:58:42,046 --> 00:58:43,845
She is a devil after all.

605
00:58:44,766 --> 00:58:46,965
Anything can come from her.

606
00:58:54,526 --> 00:58:56,325
What's the situation?

607
00:58:58,686 --> 00:59:01,005
I will remove this rock from its place.

608
00:59:01,966 --> 00:59:05,685
I will open the path to Sogut, with
Allah's permission. I will open it.

609
00:59:06,326 --> 00:59:07,445
Boran!

610
00:59:08,726 --> 00:59:10,045
Leave it.

611
00:59:10,526 --> 00:59:12,565
Leave it. Get out of there.

612
00:59:12,966 --> 00:59:14,445
I will open it, my Bey.

613
00:59:14,646 --> 00:59:19,285
Don't worry. I will open it.

614
00:59:19,726 --> 00:59:21,005
Boran!

615
00:59:21,086 --> 00:59:22,885
Don't you hear me?

616
00:59:37,086 --> 00:59:38,445
Ya Allah

617
00:59:43,686 --> 00:59:45,205
Boran

618
00:59:48,326 --> 00:59:51,805
Boran! Boran! Boran

619
00:59:54,046 --> 00:59:56,285
Boran

620
00:59:57,246 --> 00:59:59,485
Boran

621
01:00:05,086 --> 01:00:07,965
Boran. Hang on, my valiant.

622
01:00:09,166 --> 01:00:10,205
Boran

623
01:00:13,446 --> 01:00:16,805
Osman Bey Secret Tents

624
01:00:52,766 --> 01:00:55,445
What am I going to do?

625
01:00:56,766 --> 01:00:59,805
I came to you with a heart
as hard as stone, Bala.

626
01:01:01,366 --> 01:01:06,085
But you are melting my heart.

627
01:01:06,926 --> 01:01:08,925
I won't allow this.

628
01:01:12,846 --> 01:01:14,965
Bring the torch!

629
01:01:17,966 --> 01:01:23,325
Come on! Faster! Hurry!
Hold it here! Hold it here!

630
01:01:26,366 --> 01:01:29,685
Ah, you didn't listen to me!
You didn't listen to me, Boran!

631
01:01:29,686 --> 01:01:33,685
You didn't listen to me!
Come on valiants, hurry! Hurry!

632
01:01:34,286 --> 01:01:35,885
My Allah..

633
01:01:42,726 --> 01:01:45,205
His hand... His hand.

634
01:01:46,086 --> 01:01:49,525
Come on! Hurry!

635
01:01:49,846 --> 01:01:54,525
Hang on... Boran

636
01:01:57,246 --> 01:01:58,285
Boran!

637
01:01:59,366 --> 01:02:01,645
My valiant...

638
01:02:13,046 --> 01:02:18,645
He is not breathing. He is
not breathing. Boran. Boran!

639
01:02:19,046 --> 01:02:22,005
Wake up! Come on my valiant!

640
01:02:22,006 --> 01:02:24,925
Open your eyes! Don't! Come on!

641
01:02:25,566 --> 01:02:29,165
Give him water. Water! Boran.

642
01:02:29,166 --> 01:02:33,365
Come on! Come on! -Here, my Bey.

643
01:02:34,246 --> 01:02:36,125
Come on! Come on!

644
01:02:39,166 --> 01:02:42,405
Come on! Come on my valiant.

645
01:02:42,766 --> 01:02:44,645
Come on!

646
01:02:44,646 --> 01:02:45,805
Boran!

647
01:02:53,766 --> 01:02:55,325
Look at me.

648
01:02:58,526 --> 01:03:01,445
Are you alright?
Are you alright?

649
01:03:01,446 --> 01:03:07,765
I am alright, my Bey. Thank Allah.
-Come here.

650
01:03:11,406 --> 01:03:14,845
My Bey. My Bey.

651
01:03:16,366 --> 01:03:21,165
I have opened the path to Sogut, Thank Allah.

652
01:03:21,206 --> 01:03:24,885
You've opened it. And
you've opened it like a lion.

653
01:03:26,366 --> 01:03:29,085
Come on. Come on, Alps. Help.

654
01:03:29,086 --> 01:03:32,405
Get up, come on!

655
01:03:43,446 --> 01:03:47,725
Ulgen, are you alright?

656
01:03:47,966 --> 01:03:50,765
You've been thoughtful since the salaat(prayer).

657
01:03:54,406 --> 01:03:57,285
I had terrible nightmares, Bala.

658
01:03:58,446 --> 01:04:00,285
I didn't know what to do.

659
01:04:00,686 --> 01:04:03,045
What did you see, Ulgen?

660
01:04:04,726 --> 01:04:08,085
My Cerkutay and Ghazi...

661
01:04:08,686 --> 01:04:10,685
..died.

662
01:04:14,526 --> 01:04:18,565
Altuga killed them with no mercy.

663
01:04:19,166 --> 01:04:22,605
May Allah forbid that, Ulgen.
Dreams don't come true.

664
01:04:23,046 --> 01:04:25,365
Don't think of bad things.

665
01:04:26,806 --> 01:04:30,725
As long as Ghazi is with Cerkutay
Bey, they will be fine. Don't worry.

666
01:04:32,766 --> 01:04:35,125
Your nightmares will end, Ulgen.

667
01:04:35,646 --> 01:04:38,485
We will come back all
together with Allah's will.

668
01:04:38,526 --> 01:04:40,925
And go back to our tribe, God willing.

669
01:04:41,646 --> 01:04:43,085
God willing.

670
01:04:43,966 --> 01:04:45,285
God willing.

671
01:04:45,766 --> 01:04:50,325
Just think... What would Ghazi
say if he saw you upset like this?

672
01:05:26,526 --> 01:05:28,925
Because of the spy among us,

673
01:05:29,726 --> 01:05:33,525
...nobody except Beys and Shahzades will go out.

674
01:05:34,966 --> 01:05:36,885
No, it's not.

675
01:05:37,726 --> 01:05:41,365
But she always gets lost.

676
01:05:41,686 --> 01:05:44,285
Mother, did you say something?

677
01:05:44,766 --> 01:05:47,485
No, girl. I said nothing.

678
01:05:51,326 --> 01:05:52,885
Where are you going, mother?

679
01:05:52,966 --> 01:05:55,565
I'll go look around, dear. You go on.

680
01:05:55,646 --> 01:05:58,845
Mother, you shouldn't go
alone. Shall I come with you?

681
01:05:59,046 --> 01:06:01,965
I won't go far away dear. You go on.

682
01:06:07,086 --> 01:06:10,725
Come, Bala. Come.

683
01:06:11,726 --> 01:06:14,165
The vengeance shall be ended.

684
01:06:21,646 --> 01:06:24,005
Follow me silently.

685
01:06:27,486 --> 01:06:30,285
Where are you going without informing, Meryem?

686
01:06:30,606 --> 01:06:32,605
You always disappear

687
01:06:50,926 --> 01:06:53,365
What are you trying to do, Meryem?

688
01:06:53,846 --> 01:06:57,685
You came this long way to pick up herbs?

689
01:06:59,366 --> 01:07:03,965
I'm afraid. For the first time, I'm so scared.

690
01:07:04,886 --> 01:07:05,765
Why?

691
01:07:05,966 --> 01:07:12,165
You can't be the one to protect those who
killed your family and betray your parents.

692
01:07:12,286 --> 01:07:13,965
Why, Bala?

693
01:07:14,726 --> 01:07:19,205
Why didn't you give my family
affection that you give to everyone?

694
01:07:20,406 --> 01:07:23,125
Why are you forcing me to take my vengeance?

695
01:07:31,406 --> 01:07:33,045
Why?

696
01:07:51,766 --> 01:07:53,565
What are they doing?

697
01:07:54,166 --> 01:07:56,565
Why are they torturing innocent people?

698
01:08:16,126 --> 01:08:18,845
You disbelievers!

699
01:08:19,926 --> 01:08:22,404
What are they doing?

700
01:08:32,725 --> 01:08:35,085
It's forbidden to perform the salaat(prayer)!

701
01:08:35,166 --> 01:08:38,925
You have to serve Ulugan now!

702
01:08:40,406 --> 01:08:44,005
You will definitely pay for this torture!

703
01:08:47,406 --> 01:08:49,444
Shut up or I'll kill you!

704
01:08:52,486 --> 01:08:54,245
Tyrants!

705
01:08:57,566 --> 01:08:59,524
Murderers!

706
01:09:00,645 --> 01:09:02,444
Help us.

707
01:09:02,805 --> 01:09:04,645
Show mercy for us, my Allah.

708
01:09:22,886 --> 01:09:25,165
-Old man.
-My Bey.

709
01:09:25,645 --> 01:09:27,564
Old man.

710
01:09:30,685 --> 01:09:33,925
Just stop, stop. Stop, old man.

711
01:09:34,086 --> 01:09:38,045
Be quiet. Nokers shouldn't hear us.

712
01:09:38,206 --> 01:09:40,805
We all pray for salvation, my Bey.

713
01:09:40,886 --> 01:09:43,752
We're too weak to resist
against those evil Mongolians.

714
01:09:43,765 --> 01:09:44,725
Old man.

715
01:09:44,966 --> 01:09:48,805
You have to stay strong. We need that.

716
01:09:49,006 --> 01:09:53,645
They tortured us terribly, my Bey.
Elders, children and woman are miserable.

717
01:09:53,886 --> 01:09:57,365
They took down our flag and silenced the azan.

718
01:10:07,006 --> 01:10:08,765
Look, old man.

719
01:10:13,126 --> 01:10:17,005
Even if they take down our flag.

720
01:10:17,206 --> 01:10:20,565
Even if they silence the
azan of Muhammad (PBUH),

721
01:10:20,606 --> 01:10:25,005
...we will always keep mentioning Allah.

722
01:10:27,366 --> 01:10:31,045
They will see and know...

723
01:10:31,486 --> 01:10:35,765
...that neither our flag will come
down nor our azan will be silenced.

724
01:10:36,406 --> 01:10:40,125
Nor they can enslave Turks.

725
01:10:40,606 --> 01:10:42,645
Don't be worrying.

726
01:10:43,446 --> 01:10:45,885
May Allah give you a long life, my Bey.

727
01:10:46,326 --> 01:10:49,485
Thank you, thank you. Aameen.

728
01:10:51,046 --> 01:10:55,205
Son, come here.

729
01:10:56,526 --> 01:10:59,085
-Thank you. You've come on time.
-You're welcome, my Bey.

730
01:10:59,406 --> 01:11:02,445
-Come here, son.
-Alright.

731
01:11:03,446 --> 01:11:06,325
What's the situation near the tribe?

732
01:11:06,446 --> 01:11:09,085
My Bey, we made such noise

733
01:11:09,326 --> 01:11:12,725
...Ulugan will go mad when he hears about it.

734
01:11:12,966 --> 01:11:17,045
He must be thinking about what
direction we'll attack from now.

735
01:11:17,446 --> 01:11:19,005
Thank you, thank you.

736
01:11:19,086 --> 01:11:22,165
-Thank you.
-Thank you, my Bey. -Thank you, my Bey.

737
01:11:22,206 --> 01:11:27,605
My Bey, if you let me, I want to
be the one to raise our flag in Sogut.

738
01:11:28,046 --> 01:11:32,125
I'd ready to sacrifice
my life to have this honor.

739
01:11:35,806 --> 01:11:39,405
Alright. Alright.
You're right.

740
01:11:39,566 --> 01:11:45,045
For your father Bayhan Bey and
those warriors who fought for the state

741
01:11:46,566 --> 01:11:49,285
...you should do this and remember them.

742
01:11:53,046 --> 01:11:55,205
Well..

743
01:11:57,286 --> 01:11:59,685
After the big noise,

744
01:12:00,326 --> 01:12:02,085
...everything will be exposed.

745
01:12:02,326 --> 01:12:06,645
But until that time, we will act silently.

746
01:12:07,406 --> 01:12:09,285
Here we go, warriors.

747
01:12:20,446 --> 01:12:23,445
Did you find Osman, Altuga?

748
01:12:23,966 --> 01:12:25,965
No, Commander Ulugan.

749
01:12:27,606 --> 01:12:30,005
Why are you here then?

750
01:12:30,126 --> 01:12:32,685
Do you have a death wish?

751
01:12:33,846 --> 01:12:39,725
While looking for Osman, I heard that the
camps and outposts near the tribe got raided.

752
01:12:42,246 --> 01:12:48,565
They killed all the nokers.
This is Osman's doing.

753
01:12:51,806 --> 01:12:54,765
What are you saying, Altuga?

754
01:12:55,486 --> 01:12:59,765
It seems Osman is going to attack the tribe.

755
01:13:00,326 --> 01:13:02,445
He wants to break our strength.

756
01:13:05,926 --> 01:13:11,365
No. Even if you fools believe that,

757
01:13:12,686 --> 01:13:14,165
..I don't.

758
01:13:15,846 --> 01:13:20,885
If Osman were to attack the tribe,
he wouldn't have made such noise.

759
01:13:22,886 --> 01:13:26,005
Although Osman is our enemy

760
01:13:26,726 --> 01:13:29,445
...he is a smart warrior.

761
01:13:31,366 --> 01:13:34,005
He'll attack right into our heart.

762
01:13:34,046 --> 01:13:38,125
In this case, what is Osman going to do, Ulugan?

763
01:13:42,686 --> 01:13:45,005
He wants to distract us.

764
01:13:46,006 --> 01:13:48,165
He is acting wisely.

765
01:13:49,806 --> 01:13:52,165
But I won't be deceived.

766
01:13:54,846 --> 01:13:57,845
He's going to attack Sogut, obviously.

767
01:14:03,286 --> 01:14:06,645
Get prepared. We're going to Sogut.

768
01:14:21,806 --> 01:14:25,565
Bala Hatun, we've gone
too far. You aren't safe here.

769
01:14:25,886 --> 01:14:27,885
She's going towards the stream.

770
01:14:28,406 --> 01:14:30,485
Where is she going?

771
01:14:40,766 --> 01:14:43,285
Damn it.

772
01:14:44,566 --> 01:14:46,845
Where did this ache come from?

773
01:14:53,486 --> 01:14:54,845
Meryem.

774
01:14:55,246 --> 01:14:56,965
Meryem.

775
01:14:58,286 --> 01:14:59,725
Meryem.

776
01:15:00,046 --> 01:15:03,725
-Bala Hatun.
-Girl, what are you doing here?

777
01:15:04,006 --> 01:15:07,245
Are you alright? Were you crying?

778
01:15:08,166 --> 01:15:10,725
I always have headache.

779
01:15:13,086 --> 01:15:16,845
So I came to the riverbank
to pick up some herbs.

780
01:15:18,046 --> 01:15:19,325
Oh my dear.

781
01:15:19,566 --> 01:15:24,165
You should have told Shahzade Alaaddin.
He would have found some cure for you.

782
01:15:24,486 --> 01:15:28,165
He prepared a cure but it didn't work.

783
01:15:28,806 --> 01:15:32,365
You said herbs grow up in the riverbank.

784
01:15:33,806 --> 01:15:38,565
-So I came here.
-My beautiful girl...

785
01:15:39,606 --> 01:15:42,485
Does it hurt you so much?

786
01:15:46,486 --> 01:15:48,325
We're too far away.

787
01:15:48,766 --> 01:15:51,965
Why did you follow me, Bala
Hatun? We should go back.

788
01:15:52,206 --> 01:15:54,685
No, dear. We are already here now.

789
01:15:55,006 --> 01:15:58,805
Let's find the herbs and heal you. Come on.

790
01:15:58,846 --> 01:16:00,645
Bala!

791
01:16:06,806 --> 01:16:08,685
Sofia.

792
01:16:15,926 --> 01:16:17,845
Did you follow my smell, dog?

793
01:16:18,206 --> 01:16:21,925
I didn't believe when my
soldiers said they saw you.

794
01:16:23,446 --> 01:16:26,165
You came to me with your own feet, huh?

795
01:16:29,926 --> 01:16:31,885
Come on.

796
01:16:32,646 --> 01:16:34,445
Don't waste my time.

797
01:16:35,046 --> 01:16:36,405
Surrender, Bala.

798
01:16:36,806 --> 01:16:38,805
Don't you know me at all, Sofia?

799
01:16:39,366 --> 01:16:42,405
I know you more than you know yourself, Bala.

800
01:16:58,726 --> 01:17:02,525
You did it, little bird. Come to your aunt now.

801
01:17:04,006 --> 01:17:05,765
Bala!

802
01:17:07,126 --> 01:17:08,645
Surrender.

803
01:17:10,806 --> 01:17:14,765
Or I'll kill this

804
01:17:16,366 --> 01:17:18,005
..little demon.

805
01:17:18,566 --> 01:17:21,165
You snake! Leave the girl.

806
01:17:22,406 --> 01:17:25,845
This is because of me,
Bala Hatun. Because of me.

807
01:17:26,526 --> 01:17:28,125
It's not your fault, dear.

808
01:17:28,446 --> 01:17:31,445
That snake always hides behind someone!

809
01:17:38,246 --> 01:17:40,845
This is the difference
between you and me, Sofia.

810
01:17:41,406 --> 01:17:43,605
You are a coward.

811
01:17:50,766 --> 01:17:52,685
Smart move, Bala.

812
01:17:53,446 --> 01:17:55,605
But this is the end for you.

813
01:17:59,606 --> 01:18:03,205
Oh... You got a big prey, Sofia.

814
01:18:08,126 --> 01:18:10,605
But she is ours now.

815
01:18:12,326 --> 01:18:14,085
She is mine!

816
01:18:15,446 --> 01:18:19,645
Not yours, Sofia. We are together now.

817
01:18:20,446 --> 01:18:23,045
Ulugan will be happy to hear this.

818
01:18:23,526 --> 01:18:26,885
Traitors! You betrayers!

819
01:18:28,766 --> 01:18:31,805
Nokers, take both of them.

820
01:18:33,846 --> 01:18:37,485
Right, Sofia. You caught her for Ulugan.

821
01:18:44,246 --> 01:18:45,965
Of course.

822
01:18:55,926 --> 01:18:57,765
Easy.

823
01:19:00,366 --> 01:19:03,405
It's time to pay, Bala.

824
01:19:05,046 --> 01:19:08,085
We're going to my tribe.
I will make you pay there.

825
01:19:08,446 --> 01:19:10,525
Keep playing your game for now, Begum.

826
01:19:10,766 --> 01:19:12,845
It won't take long.

827
01:19:13,606 --> 01:19:18,445
No. Osman can't do anything
to us as long as we have you.

828
01:19:19,246 --> 01:19:21,365
My era has begun.

829
01:19:23,926 --> 01:19:25,445
Move.

830
01:19:43,326 --> 01:19:45,725
Where is my mother?

831
01:19:52,806 --> 01:19:57,285
-We can't find her.
-Bala is gone!

832
01:19:57,566 --> 01:20:00,085
I looked everywhere but couldn't find her.

833
01:20:00,686 --> 01:20:03,165
Sisters haven't seen him either.

834
01:20:03,726 --> 01:20:06,645
If she had gone to father, we would know.

835
01:20:06,806 --> 01:20:08,645
It must be something else.

836
01:20:08,886 --> 01:20:12,005
Meryem isn't around either.
Something happened for sure!

837
01:20:12,526 --> 01:20:17,205
Don't worry, Fatma. We'll find
Mother Bala. Alps, prepare the horses!

838
01:20:19,366 --> 01:20:22,965
Holofira, we can go look
for her. You stay in the tribe.

839
01:20:23,166 --> 01:20:26,365
-You're carrying a baby. You should be careful.
-No, Gonca.

840
01:20:26,406 --> 01:20:29,565
If I stay, it will eat my heart
out. We should look together.

841
01:20:29,726 --> 01:20:33,405
Besides, you are with me.
I will be alright. Don't worry.

842
01:20:34,086 --> 01:20:35,565
-Fine.
-Ulgen.

843
01:20:35,646 --> 01:20:39,205
You stay in the tribe and keep
security with Sisters, alright?

844
01:20:39,486 --> 01:20:41,685
You're in charge here.

845
01:21:25,846 --> 01:21:27,205
Remove these.

846
01:21:27,206 --> 01:21:28,885
They will notice us soon.

847
01:21:28,886 --> 01:21:31,885
With the noise that the
people of Sogut will hear...

848
01:21:31,886 --> 01:21:34,965
...everyone will come to the square, my Bey.
-Yes, yes.

849
01:21:35,526 --> 01:21:38,045
Come on. It is time to hunt.

850
01:22:41,846 --> 01:22:44,365
Take these. Come on!

851
01:24:44,486 --> 01:24:45,605
Come on.

852
01:24:59,646 --> 01:25:01,365
Aykurt, set the flying flames.

853
01:25:01,366 --> 01:25:03,565
You will carry them inside, come on!

854
01:25:06,766 --> 01:25:08,165
Come on.

855
01:25:25,326 --> 01:25:28,125
We will turn this place into a bloodbath today.

856
01:25:28,126 --> 01:25:30,565
For every drop of tears they shed....

857
01:25:30,726 --> 01:25:33,965
...we will take our revenge by
shedding their blood, my Bey.

858
01:25:33,966 --> 01:25:35,885
God willing, son, God willing.

859
01:25:44,966 --> 01:25:46,925
Our work isn't done yet.

860
01:25:47,446 --> 01:25:49,565
We are just beginning. Let's go.

861
01:25:54,486 --> 01:25:56,045
Osman.

862
01:26:05,606 --> 01:26:06,725
My Bey.

863
01:26:07,566 --> 01:26:09,085
The upstairs is clean.

864
01:26:09,606 --> 01:26:10,645
Okay.

865
01:26:16,646 --> 01:26:19,125
Now we know what they have been hiding.

866
01:26:22,886 --> 01:26:25,645
Nokers! Osman is here!

867
01:26:25,926 --> 01:26:29,885
They've entered the inn! Attack! Come on!

868
01:26:29,886 --> 01:26:31,605
Come on!

869
01:26:39,526 --> 01:26:42,325
My Bey, flying flames..

870
01:26:45,126 --> 01:26:50,485
The flying flames on our backs were
enough to destroy all the Mongols.

871
01:26:50,486 --> 01:26:54,445
Now imagine what will happen with these, son.

872
01:26:58,926 --> 01:27:03,405
-They surrounded the inn, my Bey.
-This is what I wanted.

873
01:27:03,406 --> 01:27:05,885
Let them come, let them come.

874
01:27:06,886 --> 01:27:09,085
Everyone knows what to do. Let's go.

875
01:27:23,166 --> 01:27:26,325
Come on!

876
01:27:26,686 --> 01:27:29,245
Osman!

877
01:27:29,246 --> 01:27:31,765
I will drown you in your own blood.

878
01:27:35,846 --> 01:27:39,725
Blood, blood, blood!

879
01:27:39,726 --> 01:27:50,405
Blood, blood, blood!

880
01:27:58,886 --> 01:28:02,565
Trap!

881
01:28:33,606 --> 01:28:35,765
The sounds come from Sogut, Ulugan.

882
01:28:35,766 --> 01:28:37,765
Osman must have attacked already!

883
01:28:40,646 --> 01:28:43,325
Hurry, let's go!

884
01:29:26,366 --> 01:29:30,365
Alps, we will search the
area thoroughly, come on!

885
01:29:34,446 --> 01:29:36,725
Aunt, these are our Alps!

886
01:29:44,566 --> 01:29:47,765
Mongols did this. It's their arrow.

887
01:29:48,406 --> 01:29:51,725
Alps, be cautious, they were ambushed.

888
01:30:06,406 --> 01:30:07,445
This..

889
01:30:09,886 --> 01:30:11,045
...is my mother's.

890
01:30:12,246 --> 01:30:14,085
This belongs to my mother, aunt.

891
01:30:16,326 --> 01:30:18,045
If we look at the tracks..

892
01:30:18,966 --> 01:30:20,925
...my mother fought with them.

893
01:30:21,326 --> 01:30:23,405
But since she is not here...

894
01:30:24,766 --> 01:30:28,285
If she could have escaped,
she would have come to the tribe.

895
01:30:31,006 --> 01:30:33,085
Apparently, they have my mother.

896
01:30:34,246 --> 01:30:36,925
My mother must be their prisoner now.

897
01:30:37,926 --> 01:30:39,925
Meryem might be with her.

898
01:30:41,806 --> 01:30:45,845
Then we need to inform
my father immediately. Alps!

899
01:30:45,926 --> 01:30:48,433
Bury the martyrs, we are
going to Sogut. Let's go.

900
01:30:48,445 --> 01:30:49,285
Let's go.

901
01:30:52,126 --> 01:30:53,605
Come on Alps!

902
01:30:54,366 --> 01:30:59,725
-Let go! Don't touch!
-Bala Hatun!

903
01:31:30,806 --> 01:31:32,165
Let go

904
01:31:36,606 --> 01:31:38,165
Kayi's people!

905
01:31:39,086 --> 01:31:43,485
If you want to see the end
of pride, look at Bala Hatun.

906
01:31:44,846 --> 01:31:48,005
Learn a lesson, look at what happened to her...

907
01:31:48,326 --> 01:31:51,365
...who once proudly walked around the tribe.

908
01:31:51,526 --> 01:31:55,445
Do you think we are defeated
because our hands are chained, Begum?

909
01:31:57,046 --> 01:31:59,805
What is a title, what is glory?

910
01:31:59,886 --> 01:32:04,045
We give our lives for our da'wah
and we are honored by that.

911
01:32:05,086 --> 01:32:06,205
But you..

912
01:32:06,526 --> 01:32:12,445
For the power, you trample on your
honor and become the lowest of the low.

913
01:32:13,126 --> 01:32:15,565
Is there a better example than you?

914
01:32:18,766 --> 01:32:22,085
You and your Bey are the same, Bala.

915
01:32:22,886 --> 01:32:27,125
You love telling the story of your
defeat as if it's a victory, right?

916
01:32:28,166 --> 01:32:30,685
But you are disgraced.

917
01:32:31,446 --> 01:32:33,285
There is no way out for you now.

918
01:32:35,926 --> 01:32:37,605
Sofia is right.

919
01:32:39,766 --> 01:32:41,205
You are defeated Bala.

920
01:32:41,766 --> 01:32:48,485
Now you will kneel before
me in front of your people!

921
01:32:59,686 --> 01:33:03,005
We lost martyrs, we fell as martyrs.

922
01:33:03,606 --> 01:33:07,165
But we never knelt, Begum.

923
01:33:09,326 --> 01:33:14,565
We drowned the oppression of
the tyrants and protected our da'wah.

924
01:33:14,566 --> 01:33:16,725
And this will never change!

925
01:33:16,726 --> 01:33:19,365
Now shut up and obey!

926
01:33:21,246 --> 01:33:23,805
Kneel

927
01:33:23,966 --> 01:33:25,845
Hold her tightly!

928
01:33:25,846 --> 01:33:30,605
Let go! Begum! I will kill you as well

929
01:33:30,606 --> 01:33:32,445
I will kill all of you!

930
01:33:38,326 --> 01:33:39,845
Let go!

931
01:33:41,126 --> 01:33:43,125
Let go! Don't touch!

932
01:33:43,406 --> 01:33:47,965
My word and my wife Begum
Hatun's word are the only decree.

933
01:33:48,046 --> 01:33:51,325
One who does not kneel
before us will surely die!

934
01:33:51,326 --> 01:33:53,845
Pull yourselves together!
-You traitor!

935
01:33:58,446 --> 01:34:03,045
O glorious people of
Kayi, we will get over this!

936
01:34:03,606 --> 01:34:06,645
We will take our tribe back from these dastards.

937
01:34:06,646 --> 01:34:10,925
The end of those who work with the
infidels and tyrants is torment, Begum!

938
01:34:10,926 --> 01:34:14,405
Torment! Let go! Don't touch!

939
01:34:15,126 --> 01:34:16,245
Enough!

940
01:34:17,366 --> 01:34:19,365
Take them to the caged tent!

941
01:34:21,086 --> 01:34:25,005
O people! Stand tall!

942
01:34:25,006 --> 01:34:26,925
Never give up hope

943
01:34:26,926 --> 01:34:29,925
Even if we fall, we will never be defeated!

944
01:34:30,486 --> 01:34:38,365
Allah is the Greatest!

945
01:34:38,806 --> 01:34:42,525
I wish I could kill her right now.

946
01:34:43,446 --> 01:34:46,205
We cannot punish Bala before Ulugan arrives.

947
01:34:48,086 --> 01:34:51,005
Where is Ulugan, Sofia?
-In Sogut.

948
01:34:51,446 --> 01:34:54,925
Osman planned a big game to take Sogut back.

949
01:34:55,886 --> 01:34:58,525
Ulugan is dealing with him.

950
01:35:00,206 --> 01:35:04,885
If Osman takes Sogut, it will be more
difficult for us to stand against him.

951
01:35:05,446 --> 01:35:08,165
Osman can do anything for Bala.

952
01:35:09,366 --> 01:35:12,045
Bala is the biggest advantage we have.

953
01:35:17,126 --> 01:35:20,565
Now, the dogs have captured Bala Hatun.

954
01:35:21,006 --> 01:35:22,525
First us...

955
01:35:22,646 --> 01:35:24,365
...now Bala Hatun.

956
01:35:31,966 --> 01:35:35,325
Father? Father, are you alright?

957
01:35:35,486 --> 01:35:39,565
Father, are you alright?
-I am, my lion.

958
01:35:40,166 --> 01:35:41,405
I am.

959
01:35:41,686 --> 01:35:42,805
Father...

960
01:35:43,446 --> 01:35:45,205
...we need to do something.

961
01:35:48,366 --> 01:35:50,325
Besides..

962
01:35:50,326 --> 01:35:54,085
...the time my uncle...

963
01:35:55,326 --> 01:36:00,285
...Altuga gave is running out.

964
01:36:01,006 --> 01:36:02,485
We will handle it.

965
01:36:02,886 --> 01:36:04,165
We will handle it.

966
01:36:06,246 --> 01:36:08,165
But no matter what...

967
01:36:10,086 --> 01:36:12,685
...we won't tell them where Osman Bey is.

968
01:36:13,646 --> 01:36:17,445
We won't tell them where Osman Bey is.

969
01:36:18,406 --> 01:36:21,205
I won't let them hurt you.

970
01:36:24,406 --> 01:36:26,005
Even if I die..

971
01:36:26,406 --> 01:36:29,085
...I will let you come
together with your mother.

972
01:36:29,326 --> 01:36:30,365
No.

973
01:36:30,966 --> 01:36:33,445
That will not happen Cerkutay Bey.

974
01:36:34,366 --> 01:36:37,085
I spent my entire childhood without you.

975
01:36:38,206 --> 01:36:41,765
Besides, you will organize my wedding.

976
01:36:44,046 --> 01:36:46,605
I will. I will.

977
01:36:54,846 --> 01:36:58,525
My Bey made sure these wooden
railings were strong back then.

978
01:36:59,326 --> 01:37:02,845
Everything my Bey does, he does it perfectly.

979
01:37:03,966 --> 01:37:06,445
I wish they were weaker.

980
01:37:07,006 --> 01:37:09,405
We could break them down and leave!

981
01:37:11,166 --> 01:37:12,725
You, Ghazi...

982
01:37:14,046 --> 01:37:16,725
You are making me laugh even in this situation.

983
01:37:19,886 --> 01:37:21,845
We will get out of here, my lion.

984
01:37:22,846 --> 01:37:24,725
We will..

985
01:37:24,726 --> 01:37:25,845
God willing.

986
01:37:32,206 --> 01:37:33,605
Slowly!

987
01:37:35,446 --> 01:37:37,885
Here.

988
01:37:51,886 --> 01:37:53,285
Dastards!

989
01:38:00,886 --> 01:38:03,205
Get in there!

990
01:38:10,126 --> 01:38:12,525
One by one, you are falling into our hands.

991
01:38:13,046 --> 01:38:14,925
Next to you...

992
01:38:14,966 --> 01:38:20,285
...we are keeping traitor
Cerkutay and his puppy.

993
01:38:21,126 --> 01:38:22,165
Come on.

994
01:38:28,086 --> 01:38:30,365
Ghazi..

995
01:38:30,366 --> 01:38:35,245
He is too young. It's all my fault...

996
01:38:35,686 --> 01:38:38,165
Why did you leave before letting us know?

997
01:38:38,966 --> 01:38:42,045
Didn't I tell you that you
won't go anywhere alone?

998
01:38:42,846 --> 01:38:45,925
That's why. Because it was dangerous...

999
01:38:46,046 --> 01:38:49,285
...I was going to leave
silently and collect the herbs.

1000
01:38:49,326 --> 01:38:50,365
If I told you..

1001
01:38:50,446 --> 01:38:52,653
...you would not allow me
and you would come with me.

1002
01:38:52,665 --> 01:38:53,405
Yes!

1003
01:38:53,406 --> 01:38:56,605
We would not leave you alone, but...
-Look, it's worse now.

1004
01:38:59,926 --> 01:39:01,725
Forgive me, Bala Hatun.

1005
01:39:07,246 --> 01:39:08,405
Anyway.

1006
01:39:09,046 --> 01:39:12,165
There must be something
good in this, my daughter.

1007
01:39:12,646 --> 01:39:14,685
What might be good right now?

1008
01:39:23,595 --> 01:39:27,555
"You may dislike something 
although it is good for you...

1009
01:39:27,555 --> 01:39:32,845
...or like something although it is bad for you
God knows and you do not"

1010
01:39:33,575 --> 01:39:35,095
Surah Al Baqarah 216

1011
01:39:39,686 --> 01:39:44,125
It's time now! Revenge!

1012
01:39:44,126 --> 01:39:47,285
It's the day of war! Come
on! Attack, people of Sogut!

1013
01:39:49,006 --> 01:39:52,405
Allah is the Greatest!

1014
01:40:23,526 --> 01:40:26,525
Do not show mercy to anyone, Alps! Don't!

1015
01:40:41,486 --> 01:40:43,005
Come on Alps!

1016
01:40:43,006 --> 01:40:48,045
Allah is the Greatest!

1017
01:40:58,886 --> 01:41:03,605
We'll sacrifice our lives
for our state! Allah-u Akbar!

1018
01:41:06,166 --> 01:41:09,405
As long as a state have such a nation

1019
01:41:09,766 --> 01:41:12,165
..it will never fall!

1020
01:41:41,286 --> 01:41:43,085
Allah is the greatest!

1021
01:41:43,366 --> 01:41:45,725
Come on, brothers!

1022
01:41:59,926 --> 01:42:01,645
Saruca!

1023
01:42:06,686 --> 01:42:09,445
Raise our glorious banner.

1024
01:42:11,806 --> 01:42:15,285
Hold on, banner. We are almost there.

1025
01:42:15,366 --> 01:42:17,765
You will wave where you belong.

1026
01:42:20,846 --> 01:42:23,445
Allah is the greatest!

1027
01:42:51,326 --> 01:42:54,805
Nokers, let's water Sogut
with the blood of Kayi!

1028
01:43:05,726 --> 01:43:08,565
Hearing that you are a prisoner,

1029
01:43:09,086 --> 01:43:11,485
...Osman Bey won't stop, right?

1030
01:43:13,446 --> 01:43:15,325
What if he surrenders?

1031
01:43:15,686 --> 01:43:17,445
I won't let that happen.

1032
01:43:17,926 --> 01:43:19,725
We'll get out of here, Meryem.

1033
01:43:20,206 --> 01:43:21,445
How?

1034
01:43:21,846 --> 01:43:25,765
They think they are the predators
and we are the preys, huh?

1035
01:43:26,766 --> 01:43:31,045
But as the deer knows the
mountain, the hunter will be hunted.

1036
01:43:32,006 --> 01:43:34,165
This is our tribe, my girl.

1037
01:43:34,686 --> 01:43:36,285
We'll get out of here.

1038
01:43:47,086 --> 01:43:48,485
Bala.

1039
01:43:50,366 --> 01:43:53,205
I hope you don't feel uncomfortable.

1040
01:43:53,966 --> 01:43:56,005
You vile dog.

1041
01:44:06,046 --> 01:44:08,205
Why would I feel uncomfortable?

1042
01:44:08,326 --> 01:44:10,045
This is my tribe.

1043
01:44:10,486 --> 01:44:13,325
I will send you where you deserve, Begum.

1044
01:44:14,286 --> 01:44:16,765
You can't overpower me, Bala.

1045
01:44:17,206 --> 01:44:23,605
Look. Your people, tent
and tribe... They are all mine.

1046
01:44:24,686 --> 01:44:27,685
And you are my prisoner.

1047
01:44:28,446 --> 01:44:31,205
Come closer. Are you afraid?

1048
01:44:31,926 --> 01:44:34,045
You say this is your tribe.

1049
01:44:34,486 --> 01:44:36,965
Your wound is in so deep, right, Begum?

1050
01:44:37,526 --> 01:44:42,365
My tribe, my tent and people...
I will take all of them back.

1051
01:44:44,246 --> 01:44:47,325
But there is something you can't take from me.

1052
01:45:09,766 --> 01:45:11,325
What is it?

1053
01:45:11,726 --> 01:45:18,365
You'll never be able to take my
husband, my love and my place, Begum.

1054
01:45:18,806 --> 01:45:20,645
Ever.

1055
01:45:23,166 --> 01:45:25,725
Are you angry, Begum?

1056
01:45:44,806 --> 01:45:49,285
This slap is not for you but for the
cruelty you showed against my people.

1057
01:45:56,566 --> 01:46:00,885
Filthy woman! Come on,
Meryem. Let's find Cerkutay.

1058
01:46:47,286 --> 01:46:49,245
My boy.

1059
01:46:51,086 --> 01:46:54,525
-Father.
My brave boy.

1060
01:46:55,886 --> 01:46:57,765
I'm very hungry.

1061
01:46:58,406 --> 01:47:00,285
Starving

1062
01:47:01,526 --> 01:47:03,965
As hungry as a wolf.

1063
01:47:06,966 --> 01:47:08,605
Bala Hatun.

1064
01:47:12,006 --> 01:47:14,845
Bala... Bala Hatun.
-Ghazi.

1065
01:47:17,606 --> 01:47:19,525
We'll be saved.

1066
01:47:21,726 --> 01:47:24,445
Close the door.
Close the door, girl.

1067
01:47:26,726 --> 01:47:28,285
Bala Hatun.

1068
01:47:29,086 --> 01:47:30,325
Bala Hatun.

1069
01:47:30,486 --> 01:47:33,005
-Are you alright?
-We're good.

1070
01:47:35,006 --> 01:47:38,245
We have to get out of
here quickly. Let's get out.

1071
01:47:41,806 --> 01:47:44,205
They may notice any moment.

1072
01:47:50,246 --> 01:47:53,925
-Come on, Ghazi.
-Ghazi, stick to Meryem.

1073
01:47:54,086 --> 01:47:56,405
Ghazi. Cerkutay.

1074
01:47:59,086 --> 01:48:01,005
Let's go.

1075
01:48:05,086 --> 01:48:07,685
Nokers, catch her! She's running off!

1076
01:48:07,726 --> 01:48:09,845
Run and never look behind!

1077
01:48:14,166 --> 01:48:17,485
-Meryem, take this. Run! Run!
-Come on.

1078
01:48:24,846 --> 01:48:26,485
Don't let them escape!

1079
01:48:26,846 --> 01:48:28,845
Catch them, come on!

1080
01:48:32,966 --> 01:48:36,045
Come here, dastards.

1081
01:48:37,926 --> 01:48:42,525
Whoever did this to my homeland
I will cut off their arms and legs!

1082
01:48:58,886 --> 01:49:02,805
-We'll break them all, brother!
-For sure, brother!

1083
01:49:03,046 --> 01:49:05,085
For sure!

1084
01:49:06,646 --> 01:49:10,685
We'll make all of them regret
that they came to the frontiers!

1085
01:49:10,846 --> 01:49:12,765
Ya Allah!

1086
01:49:25,686 --> 01:49:28,125
Come on, brothers! Come on!

1087
01:49:30,326 --> 01:49:33,565
We'll eradicate these dogs! Come on!

1088
01:49:56,486 --> 01:49:58,405
Thank you, my Bey!

1089
01:50:15,366 --> 01:50:17,045
Saruca

1090
01:50:20,606 --> 01:50:23,245
Boran Bey, protect Saruca!

1091
01:50:28,126 --> 01:50:32,365
Even if you break my arms and
wings... Even if you take out my heart.

1092
01:50:32,686 --> 01:50:35,085
...this flag will wave!

1093
01:50:43,726 --> 01:50:45,805
Saruca.

1094
01:50:47,206 --> 01:50:51,005
Praise be, my warrior. Praise be.

1095
01:50:55,046 --> 01:51:05,045
Allah is the greatest!

1096
01:51:05,766 --> 01:51:07,525
Allah is the greatest!

1097
01:51:13,486 --> 01:51:17,485
Ulugan, forgive me but...

1098
01:51:18,646 --> 01:51:21,445
Why are we glad as if we were victorious?

1099
01:51:21,526 --> 01:51:24,565
Why don't we fight?
-They...

1100
01:51:25,126 --> 01:51:27,605
...are fighting in vain, Altuga.

1101
01:51:27,966 --> 01:51:32,485
A gazelle's struggle in a hyena's paw.

1102
01:51:34,046 --> 01:51:38,765
Osman just shaved my beard by capturing Sogut.

1103
01:51:39,246 --> 01:51:42,645
But I will cut off his head.

1104
01:51:43,166 --> 01:51:46,903
We're losing Sogut, Ulugan.
When Olcaytu hears this...

1105
01:51:46,915 --> 01:51:48,165
Shut up, Altuga.

1106
01:51:48,366 --> 01:51:50,645
You don't see the future.

1107
01:51:51,086 --> 01:51:53,965
I'm holding Osman's heart in my hand.

1108
01:51:54,526 --> 01:51:56,925
As long as I have his tribe

1109
01:51:57,126 --> 01:52:04,405
...he'll fall into my trap sooner
or later and beg me like a dog.

1110
01:52:05,286 --> 01:52:09,205
Then we will be victorious.

1111
01:52:10,206 --> 01:52:12,525
We'll be victorious.

1112
01:52:17,366 --> 01:52:19,645
You can't go anywhere, Bala.

1113
01:52:24,686 --> 01:52:27,045
Come on, people!

1114
01:53:07,886 --> 01:53:11,805
Horses are here, Bala Hatun.
Alaca is here too. Come on!

1115
01:53:12,966 --> 01:53:15,445
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

1116
01:53:23,806 --> 01:53:25,125
My Alaca.

1117
01:53:25,366 --> 01:53:29,725
-Ilbay, do something. They're escaping.
-Bring the horses!

1118
01:53:32,006 --> 01:53:33,565
Let's go.

1119
01:53:34,966 --> 01:53:36,725
We won't let you catch Bala!

1120
01:53:36,886 --> 01:53:40,965
I will come back and take
our tribe back. Don't worry!

1121
01:53:43,446 --> 01:53:46,125
Come on! Come on!

1122
01:53:54,526 --> 01:53:56,365
People!

1123
01:53:56,886 --> 01:53:59,525
You are betraying your kin!

1124
01:53:59,686 --> 01:54:01,885
If you stand against me,

1125
01:54:02,046 --> 01:54:06,245
...I will kill everyone
including women and children!

1126
01:54:06,406 --> 01:54:07,965
I swear!

1127
01:54:14,446 --> 01:54:16,245
Come on.

1128
01:55:22,766 --> 01:55:26,005
There is no god but Allah.

1129
01:55:31,566 --> 01:55:37,485
Old man, don't do this.
Don't embarrass me. Please.

1130
01:55:39,406 --> 01:55:41,525
May Allah be pleased with you, my Bey.

1131
01:55:41,966 --> 01:55:44,525
You didn't let us be slaves for the enemy.

1132
01:55:44,926 --> 01:55:47,325
May Allah give you such a gift...

1133
01:55:47,686 --> 01:55:50,205
...that your name will
spread all around the world.

1134
01:55:50,406 --> 01:55:52,765
That your generations will prevail.

1135
01:55:53,086 --> 01:55:57,085
That your children will have reputation
and keep the order in the world.

1136
01:55:57,846 --> 01:56:00,525
Old man, don't.

1137
01:56:01,166 --> 01:56:03,765
I don't seek praise here.

1138
01:56:04,086 --> 01:56:05,885
I don't want that.

1139
01:56:05,926 --> 01:56:09,405
I just intend to spread Allah's religion.

1140
01:56:09,446 --> 01:56:12,085
And provide peace and order here.

1141
01:56:12,886 --> 01:56:18,085
My boy, the brave should be praised.

1142
01:56:18,726 --> 01:56:21,285
May Allah be very pleased with you.

1143
01:56:22,286 --> 01:56:23,805
Thank you.

1144
01:56:24,446 --> 01:56:25,965
Thank you.

1145
01:56:31,726 --> 01:56:33,365
My Beys.

1146
01:56:34,046 --> 01:56:35,525
My alps.

1147
01:56:36,486 --> 01:56:41,965
I took vengeance and kept my promise.

1148
01:56:42,846 --> 01:56:46,565
I never abandoned the
right path for my comfort...

1149
01:56:47,086 --> 01:56:52,485
...or bowed against cowards,
dastards and betrayers!

1150
01:56:54,406 --> 01:56:58,685
I never sold our freedom for coins!

1151
01:57:00,406 --> 01:57:04,645
Now... I swear on this smoke...

1152
01:57:04,966 --> 01:57:11,045
...that we will never give up
fighting as long as I keep breathing

1153
01:57:11,126 --> 01:57:14,045
-We will never give up!
-Allah is the greatest!

1154
01:57:14,166 --> 01:57:15,685
Allah-u Akbar!

1155
01:57:15,726 --> 01:57:21,045
-Allah is the greatest!
-Allah is the greatest!

1156
01:57:23,486 --> 01:57:25,885
Father!

1157
01:57:26,806 --> 01:57:27,845
Father!

1158
01:57:29,646 --> 01:57:30,765
Father.

1159
01:57:31,446 --> 01:57:32,525
My daughter...

1160
01:57:32,646 --> 01:57:37,925
-Father! My mother...
What happened to your mother?

1161
01:57:38,326 --> 01:57:40,325
They abducted my mother, father.

1162
01:57:40,886 --> 01:57:43,005
Nokers took my mother away!

1163
01:57:43,486 --> 01:57:45,405
How?

1164
01:57:47,806 --> 01:57:49,445
What?

1165
01:57:50,166 --> 01:57:51,965
How? How?

1166
01:57:52,166 --> 01:57:55,005
We don't know how, father.
But we followed their tracks.

1167
01:57:55,006 --> 01:57:56,445
They led us to the tribe.

1168
01:58:02,806 --> 01:58:06,765
Bring my horse here!
-Alps! Hurry! Now!

1169
01:58:07,086 --> 01:58:08,605
You stay here.

1170
01:58:08,646 --> 01:58:10,485
Close the doors.

1171
01:58:12,206 --> 01:58:13,445
My sons.

1172
01:58:13,926 --> 01:58:14,965
Come on.

1173
01:58:19,486 --> 01:58:21,085
Ya Allah..

1174
01:58:41,046 --> 01:58:43,005
Come on!

1175
01:58:50,726 --> 01:58:52,605
Bala Hatun.

1176
01:58:52,646 --> 01:58:55,925
-Bala Hatun. Bala Hatun.
-Cerkutay.

1177
01:58:58,446 --> 01:59:00,485
You take Ghazi and Meryem. And leave.

1178
01:59:00,486 --> 01:59:02,045
I will waste their time.

1179
01:59:02,046 --> 01:59:05,245
No. No. We will go together.
-Bala Hatun.

1180
01:59:06,246 --> 01:59:07,765
This is the best way.

1181
01:59:12,526 --> 01:59:14,285
Run and survive.

1182
01:59:15,446 --> 01:59:16,485
Good.

1183
01:59:16,606 --> 01:59:20,925
Come on Ghazi. Come on my lion. Go to Bala.

1184
01:59:20,926 --> 01:59:26,645
-Come on. May Allah help you.
-You too, Cerkutay.

1185
01:59:26,646 --> 01:59:27,845
Be careful.

1186
01:59:28,406 --> 01:59:32,445
Come on! Come on Alaca!
Show us how fast you are!

1187
01:59:32,726 --> 01:59:33,845
Let's go!

1188
01:59:37,766 --> 01:59:39,325
Bala Hatun.

1189
01:59:39,686 --> 01:59:40,405
Come on!

1190
01:59:40,405 --> 01:59:42,365
I know a way! Come with me! This way!

1191
01:59:42,366 --> 01:59:44,045
Come with me!

1192
01:59:44,046 --> 01:59:46,365
We found them! Come on!

1193
01:59:52,206 --> 01:59:56,125
This way! Come on! -Begum Hatun!

1194
01:59:56,406 --> 01:59:58,525
Come on. -You go.

1195
01:59:58,526 --> 02:00:00,165
I will go there from behind.

1196
02:00:02,446 --> 02:00:03,685
Come on

1197
02:00:10,726 --> 02:00:13,405
I will not fall for the game you are playing.

1198
02:00:13,566 --> 02:00:16,325
You will die today Bala. Come on!

1199
02:00:30,046 --> 02:00:33,645
My Allah, do not test me with my love...

1200
02:00:42,686 --> 02:00:44,365
Come on!

1201
02:00:49,366 --> 02:00:53,565
Bala Hatun!

1202
02:00:53,566 --> 02:00:56,205
Bala Hatun are you alright?
-I am alright, Ghazi.

1203
02:00:56,206 --> 02:00:57,325
I am alright. Come on!

1204
02:01:01,686 --> 02:01:03,205
Bala Hatun!

1205
02:01:04,926 --> 02:01:07,565
Are you alright? -I am alright.

1206
02:01:10,686 --> 02:01:12,005
Dastards...

1207
02:01:13,086 --> 02:01:14,885
Be careful Bala Hatun.

1208
02:01:17,206 --> 02:01:21,045
Ghazi. Go with your Meryem sister.

1209
02:01:21,046 --> 02:01:23,445
-Come on, Meryem, get off the horse.
-No, Bala Hatun.

1210
02:01:23,446 --> 02:01:25,285
-No, I won't leave you alone.
-Ghazi..

1211
02:01:25,286 --> 02:01:27,165
Go and save yourself. She wants me.

1212
02:01:27,166 --> 02:01:29,165
Come on, my son. Come on!

1213
02:01:31,886 --> 02:01:34,005
Run now! Go!

1214
02:01:38,806 --> 02:01:40,485
Go!

1215
02:01:43,446 --> 02:01:45,085
Hurry!

1216
02:01:49,246 --> 02:01:51,445
You don't have any breath left to take!

1217
02:01:51,446 --> 02:01:53,085
Don't run away! Come here, Bala!

1218
02:02:01,846 --> 02:02:04,885
Come on Iltutan! Come on! Bala!

1219
02:02:05,726 --> 02:02:07,405
I am coming, Bala!

1220
02:02:08,686 --> 02:02:10,525
I am coming Bala!

1221
02:02:28,646 --> 02:02:30,085
Come on, my girl

1222
02:02:30,086 --> 02:02:34,405
Come on.

1223
02:02:36,926 --> 02:02:38,885
Stop.

1224
02:02:46,606 --> 02:02:49,325
Come, my Alaca. Come.

1225
02:02:58,606 --> 02:03:01,125
Look everywhere, don't let her escape!

1226
02:04:54,366 --> 02:04:57,285
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

1227
02:05:13,246 --> 02:05:15,045
Bala..

1228
02:05:24,046 --> 02:05:26,085
Come.

1229
02:05:33,566 --> 02:05:35,885
Neither Ulugan, nor Osman.

1230
02:05:36,086 --> 02:05:37,885
I won't wait for anyone.

1231
02:05:38,126 --> 02:05:40,205
You will die today, Bala.

1232
02:05:47,846 --> 02:05:49,085
Begum..

1233
02:05:53,286 --> 02:05:54,485
Move!

1234
02:05:58,326 --> 02:05:59,565
I said move!

1235
02:06:01,846 --> 02:06:03,925
So that you love Bala so much...

1236
02:06:04,246 --> 02:06:05,645
...then you must die as well

1237
02:06:08,366 --> 02:06:10,805
Alaca! My Alaca!

1238
02:06:11,686 --> 02:06:13,565
Don't worry Bala...

1239
02:06:14,926 --> 02:06:18,165
You don't need a horse anymore.
-Begum...

1240
02:06:18,166 --> 02:06:21,205
I will kill you Begum. I will kill you!

1241
02:06:22,446 --> 02:06:25,125
Come on Meryem! Come on!

1242
02:06:25,126 --> 02:06:30,445
We must find Bala Hatun! Come on!
-Ghazi! Ghazi!

1243
02:06:30,446 --> 02:06:31,925
Ghazi, what are you doing?

1244
02:06:31,926 --> 02:06:34,925
Bala Hatun let them chase her for us!

1245
02:06:35,126 --> 02:06:36,405
Where are you going?

1246
02:06:36,406 --> 02:06:39,885
That's better! Bala Hatun
risked her own life for us!

1247
02:06:39,886 --> 02:06:41,805
Now it's our turn Meryem!

1248
02:06:41,846 --> 02:06:43,525
We must find her!

1249
02:06:43,646 --> 02:06:45,685
What can you even do to them, Ghazi?

1250
02:06:45,686 --> 02:06:47,765
Anything for Bala Hatun!

1251
02:06:48,086 --> 02:06:50,565
Come on Meryem! We must go there!

1252
02:06:50,766 --> 02:06:54,125
Come on!

1253
02:06:54,126 --> 02:06:55,725
Make your decision, Meryem.

1254
02:06:55,726 --> 02:06:58,725
You will either come with me or stay here!

1255
02:07:05,006 --> 02:07:06,445
Damn it!

1256
02:07:24,206 --> 02:07:27,445
I swear, I will kill you Begum!

1257
02:07:27,446 --> 02:07:29,205
You will pay for your betrayal!

1258
02:07:29,206 --> 02:07:31,285
I became a traitor because of you!

1259
02:07:31,286 --> 02:07:33,525
If you hadn't come, Osman...

1260
02:07:33,526 --> 02:07:35,765
Don't you say my husband's name again!

1261
02:07:47,006 --> 02:07:48,165
You are...

1262
02:07:48,566 --> 02:07:52,125
...a traitor who betrayed her state!

1263
02:07:52,126 --> 02:07:54,125
You are a traitor...

1264
02:07:54,126 --> 02:07:57,885
...who betrayed her brother!

1265
02:07:58,166 --> 02:08:01,085
You cannot defeat me Bala!

1266
02:08:12,246 --> 02:08:17,405
This fire will kill you, Bala.

1267
02:08:28,086 --> 02:08:31,685
I ripped out your heart, Osman. Now it's over.

1268
02:08:32,886 --> 02:08:34,445
Your Bala is gone.

1269
02:08:37,766 --> 02:08:40,845
-We could not find her. -I did.

1270
02:08:47,486 --> 02:08:51,605
I, Begum Hatun, took my revenge.

1271
02:08:52,206 --> 02:08:57,725
I punished the woman who disgraced
me and sent me away from my tribe.

1272
02:08:57,726 --> 02:08:59,206
I killed Bala.

1273
02:09:00,206 --> 02:09:01,365
No..

1274
02:09:03,086 --> 02:09:04,125
No...

1275
02:09:19,726 --> 02:09:22,685
I will save Bala Hatun!

1276
02:09:22,686 --> 02:09:24,805
No Ghazi. Ghazi, no.

1277
02:09:26,126 --> 02:09:27,525
They will catch us!

1278
02:09:27,526 --> 02:09:29,405
We cannot do anything to them!

1279
02:09:35,046 --> 02:09:36,365
You are right.

1280
02:09:36,926 --> 02:09:39,845
You are right.

1281
02:09:39,846 --> 02:09:41,485
We cannot do anything.

1282
02:09:41,486 --> 02:09:43,285
We cannot do anything, Meryem.

1283
02:09:44,166 --> 02:09:45,845
But my father can.

1284
02:09:46,606 --> 02:09:49,233
My father can, Meryem. I
will go and find my father!

1285
02:09:49,245 --> 02:09:50,125
Ghazi, no.

1286
02:09:51,206 --> 02:09:52,565
Ghazi stop!

1287
02:10:24,086 --> 02:10:25,685
Alaca..

1288
02:10:31,006 --> 02:10:32,045
Mother!

1289
02:10:32,486 --> 02:10:33,525
Mother!

1290
02:10:39,006 --> 02:10:42,205
Alaca, what happened to you?

1291
02:10:42,766 --> 02:10:44,645
Bala...

1292
02:10:47,606 --> 02:10:49,245
Where are you, mother?

1293
02:10:57,006 --> 02:11:00,725
My Bey, the bloodstains of Alaca lead this way.

1294
02:11:00,726 --> 02:11:01,965
Come on Alps!

1295
02:11:08,646 --> 02:11:10,445
Come on!

1296
02:11:36,246 --> 02:11:38,885
Traitor! Begum!

1297
02:11:39,126 --> 02:11:41,765
Begum!

1298
02:11:47,206 --> 02:11:50,085
May this fire grow even stronger, Bala.

1299
02:11:52,486 --> 02:11:55,645
Stay here, and make sure
that Bala turns into ashes.

1300
02:12:00,926 --> 02:12:02,045
My Allah..

1301
02:12:02,326 --> 02:12:03,885
My Allah, help me!

1302
02:12:04,326 --> 02:12:05,525
Osman!

1303
02:12:15,486 --> 02:12:18,045
My children!

1304
02:12:24,606 --> 02:12:26,845
Osman!

1305
02:12:33,846 --> 02:12:35,605
Come on.

1306
02:12:45,446 --> 02:12:48,125
I bear witness that there
is no god but Allah... Ozgtir.

1307
02:12:52,966 --> 02:13:01,325
...and I bear witness that
Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.

1308
02:13:12,246 --> 02:13:13,965
It's over, Bala.

1309
02:13:17,126 --> 02:13:19,045
It's over.

1310
02:13:23,886 --> 02:13:25,685
You're dead.

1311
02:13:27,006 --> 02:13:28,685
And it's over.

1312
02:13:41,366 --> 02:13:43,485
If it's over,

1313
02:13:45,566 --> 02:13:48,485
...why does it hurt me so much?

1314
02:13:53,566 --> 02:13:58,925
Osman Bey! My Bey! Help, my Bey!

1315
02:14:00,166 --> 02:14:02,365
-Osman Bey.
-Ghazi.

1316
02:14:02,446 --> 02:14:05,085
-Osman Bey.
-What's going on?

1317
02:14:05,246 --> 02:14:07,045
What happened?

1318
02:14:07,166 --> 02:14:11,845
-What?
-Bala Hatun is burning in the cabin, my Bey!

1319
02:14:20,606 --> 02:14:24,045
What are you talking about? Where?

1320
02:14:24,286 --> 02:14:26,325
In the cabin ahead, my Bey.

1321
02:14:26,366 --> 02:14:30,325
-Bala...
-Help, my Bey. Bala Hatun is burning

1322
02:14:32,006 --> 02:14:35,125
-Alps!
-Let's go.

1323
02:14:37,286 --> 02:14:39,205
Come on!

1324
02:14:43,686 --> 02:14:45,685
Come on!

1325
02:14:50,726 --> 02:14:52,525
Come on!

1326
02:14:59,046 --> 02:15:01,285
Bala? Where is Bala?

1327
02:15:02,166 --> 02:15:05,485
-No.
-Wait, my Bey!

1328
02:15:07,046 --> 02:15:08,245
Bala?

1329
02:15:08,366 --> 02:15:12,365
Bala! No! Bala!

1330
02:15:12,566 --> 02:15:15,765
No! This can’t happen!

1331
02:15:17,326 --> 02:15:19,965
-Mother!
-Leave me!

1332
02:15:20,006 --> 02:15:23,485
-Leave me! Mother!
-My Shahzade!

1333
02:15:23,486 --> 02:15:25,045
Mother!

1334
02:15:32,326 --> 02:15:35,285
-What is this?
-Leave me!

1335
02:15:35,406 --> 02:15:38,005
-My Shahzade.
-Leave me! Mother!

1336
02:15:38,086 --> 02:15:40,725
-Mother!
-What is this, my Allah?

1337
02:15:40,766 --> 02:15:44,085
Bala. Don't worry. Don't worry.

1338
02:15:56,806 --> 02:15:58,805
This can't be happening.

1339
02:15:59,566 --> 02:16:02,325
No. No.

1340
02:16:03,286 --> 02:16:07,525
Leave me! Leave me! Mother!

1341
02:16:07,646 --> 02:16:10,725
I said leave me!

1342
02:16:11,326 --> 02:16:13,965
This can't be happening.

1343
02:16:17,086 --> 02:16:19,005
No.

1344
02:16:19,326 --> 02:16:23,325
This isn't real.
This isn't real.

1345
02:16:28,566 --> 02:16:32,725
Bala!

1346
02:16:36,366 --> 02:16:39,764
No!

1347
02:16:40,206 --> 02:16:44,285
Leave me! My mother is in those flames!

1348
02:16:44,366 --> 02:16:48,285
-My Shahzade.
-Leave me! Mother!

1349
02:16:52,766 --> 02:16:54,924
What have they done to us?

1350
02:16:55,966 --> 02:16:58,445
What have they done to us?

1351
02:16:59,806 --> 02:17:02,445
What have they done, Bala?

1352
02:17:03,766 --> 02:17:07,365
What have those heathens done?

1353
02:17:09,366 --> 02:17:11,805
What have you done?

1354
02:17:12,406 --> 02:17:14,565
What have you done?

1355
02:17:16,366 --> 02:17:18,485
You heathens!

1356
02:17:19,806 --> 02:17:21,125
Mother!

1357
02:17:21,286 --> 02:17:27,924
Now this fire will be my fire.

1358
02:17:28,606 --> 02:17:33,605
These flames will be my flames.

1359
02:17:48,366 --> 02:17:51,165
Mother! Leave me!

1360
02:17:51,366 --> 02:17:54,325
-My Shahzade.
-Mother!

1361
02:17:54,806 --> 02:17:56,684
Bala.

1362
02:17:57,165 --> 02:18:00,125
Fire in every ash of yours..

1363
02:18:00,366 --> 02:18:04,365
...will become your flames one by one.

1364
02:18:04,486 --> 02:18:08,725
From now on, death is forbidden for me

1365
02:18:09,846 --> 02:18:12,965
and life is forbidden for you!